      "bibliographicCitation": "Collected Works (German / Fischer Verlag)\n\n[1987]: Fischer Verlag, Frankfurt am Main\n\nRomain Rolland. Edited with an afterword by Knut Beck. 434/(4)p. 2,000 Expl. \n\nContents:\n\nBrief an Romain Rolland, pp. (9)-(19) [Berliner Tageblatt [Berlin], 22 December 1912]\nRomain Rolland und der Ruhm, pp. (21)-35 [Neue Freie Presse [Wien], 20 March 1914]\nRomain Rolland. Der Mann und das Werk, pp. (37)-(349) [Frankfurt am Main: Literarische Anstalt Rütten & Loening, 1921/1923/1926/1929]\nRomain Rollands neuer Roman, pp. (351)-(359) [Neue Freie Presse [Wien], 2 December 1923, pp. 33-35]\nDank an Romain Rolland, pp. (361)-(365) [Neue Freie Presse [Wien], 24 January 1926]\nRomain Rolland. Vortrag, gehalten im Meistersaal zu Berlin, Sonnabend, den 29. Januar 1926, pp. (367)-(388)\nRomain Rolland. Geheimnis der Produktion. Notizen zu einem Vortrag, pp. (389)-(394) [Die literarische Welt [Berlin], 26 January 1926]\nRomain Rolland, pp. (395)-(399) [January 1926. This is the first printing]\nRomain Rolland. Zum 70. Geburtstag, pp. (401)-(407) [Commune [Paris], March 1936]\nDank an Romain Rolland. Zum siebzigsten Geburtstag des Dichters, pp. (409)-(416) [Pester Lloyd [Budapest], 26 January 1936]\nNachbemerkung des Herausgebers Knut Beck], pp. (417)-(435)\nBibliographischer Nachweis, pp. (437)-(438). In his afterword, pp. 423-428, Knut Beck reprints five letters in German translation between Emile Verhaeren and Romain Rolland which Zweig had published with annotations in some Swiss newspaper. They were then reprinted in the Neues Wiener Journal [Wien], 16 July 1919: Verhaeren to Rolland, 24 October 1914; Rolland to Verhaeren, 23 November 1914; Verhaeren to Rolland, 3 December 1914; Rolland to Verhaeren, 14 June 1915; Verhaeren to Rolland, 19 June 1915\n\nFischer Editions/Reprints\n\nS. Fischer Verlag [Gesammelte Werke in Einzelbänden]\n\n*1. Auflage. 2,000 Expl. 1987\n\nKassette V: Stefan Zweig - Ein großer Europäer: Erzähler - Essayist - Dramatiker [5]\n*1. Auflage. 1,000 Expl. 1987\n\nHistorical Studies / Volumes (French)\n\n[2000]: Éditions Belfond, Paris\n\nRomain Rolland [Romain Rolland. Der Mann und das Werk]. Translated by Odette Richez (Éditions Pittoresques 1929). Text revised by Serge Niémetz. Preface by Serge Niémetz. Cover photograph of Romain Rolland © Collection Viollet. 371/(8)p. Reprinted: 381/(2)p. Same cover photograph. Paris: Éditions Belfond, 2003. Serge Niémetz. “Préface”, pp. 7-(35)\n\nContents:\n\n“Préface, pp. 7-(34)\nBiographie, pp. (37)-(86)\nDébuts dramatiques, pp. (87)-(148)\nLes Vies des hommes illustres, pp. (149)-(170)\nJean-Christophe, pp. (171)-(243)\nIntermezzo scherzoso, pp. (245)-(257)\nLa Conscience de l'Europe, pp. (259)-(351)\nDe 1919 a 1925 [Written in 1926], pp. (353)-(368)\nTable, pp. 369-(372)\n\nExcerpt:\n\n“Eloge de Romain Rolland” [“Conclusion”, p. 269 in the 1929 edition. Translated by O. Richez. 286/(1)p. Paris: Les Editions Pittoresques] in LA2 Bulletin SZ, No. 19 (Jan./Feb. 1998), p. 21 [“Conclusion”, pp. 359-(360) in the 2003 edition]",
      "sourceBlobId": 5
