      ],
      "mainCategory": "Fiction",
      "hasPart": [
        "A. The quotations, which are extracted primarily from Zweig’s fiction and his ‘Sternstunden der Menschheit’ [71 sources quoted], are divided into the following categories:",
        "Shehui [Society]. 5 quotations, pp. 1-28",
        "Jieji [Class]. 3 quotations, pp. 29-38",
        "Minzu [Ethnicity]. 2 quotations, pp. 39-44",
        "Jinbu [Progress]. 4 quotations, pp. 45-66",
        "Rensheng [Meaning of life]. 7 quotations, pp. 67-94",
        "Weida [Greatness]. 3 quotations, pp. 95-112",
        "Sixiang [Thought]. 3 quotations, pp. 113-120",
        "Xiji [Aspirations]. 3 quotations, pp. 121-130",
        "Ziqiang [Self-development]. 4 quotations, pp. 131-138",
        "Jinyi [Courage / perseverance]. 3 quotations, pp. 139-150",
        "Pinde [Moral character]. 2 quotations, pp. 151-158",
        "Chushi [Social conduct]. 7 quotations, pp. 159-188",
        "Xinfu [Happiness]. 2 quotations, pp. 189-204",
        "Chengbai [Success and failure]. 1 quotation, pp.205-210",
        "Shengming [Fate]. 5 quotations, pp. 211-226",
        "Funü [Women]. 2 quotations, pp. 227-234",
        "Aiqing [Love]. 6 quotations, pp. 235-270",
        "Zheli [Philosophy]. 3 quotations, pp. 271-278",
        "Zhishi [Knowledge]. 3 quotations, pp. 279-290",
        "Wenyi [Literature and art]. 3 quotations, pp. 291-304"
      ],
      "bibliographicCitation": "[1991]: Ganshu Renmin Chubanshe, Lanzhou\n\nCiweige miao yulu [Brilliant Quotations from Zweig’s Works]. Compiled with a chronological afterword by Wen Qi. 307p. \n\nContents:\n\nA. The quotations, which are extracted primarily from Zweig’s fiction and his ‘Sternstunden der Menschheit’ [71 sources quoted], are divided into the following categories:\n\nShehui [Society]. 5 quotations, pp. 1-28\nJieji [Class]. 3 quotations, pp. 29-38\nMinzu [Ethnicity]. 2 quotations, pp. 39-44\nJinbu [Progress]. 4 quotations, pp. 45-66\nRensheng [Meaning of life]. 7 quotations, pp. 67-94\nWeida [Greatness]. 3 quotations, pp. 95-112\nSixiang [Thought]. 3 quotations, pp. 113-120\nXiji [Aspirations]. 3 quotations, pp. 121-130\nZiqiang [Self-development]. 4 quotations, pp. 131-138\nJinyi [Courage / perseverance]. 3 quotations, pp. 139-150\nPinde [Moral character]. 2 quotations, pp. 151-158\nChushi [Social conduct]. 7 quotations, pp. 159-188\nXinfu [Happiness]. 2 quotations, pp. 189-204\nChengbai [Success and failure]. 1 quotation, pp.205-210\nShengming [Fate]. 5 quotations, pp. 211-226\nFunü [Women]. 2 quotations, pp. 227-234\nAiqing [Love]. 6 quotations, pp. 235-270\nZheli [Philosophy]. 3 quotations, pp. 271-278\nZhishi [Knowledge]. 3 quotations, pp. 279-290\nWenyi [Literature and art]. 3 quotations, pp. 291-304\n\nB. The quotations are taken from the following works:\n\nYidui kusi er you huiyi de luansheng jiemei [Die gleich-ungleichen Schwestern]\nYike xin de lunsang [Untergang eines Herzens]\nYin taowang er ming chui giangu [Flucht in die Unsterblichkeit]\nXiangqi de gushi [Schachnovelle]\nSanren shujian [Der Briefwechsel von Maxim Gorki, Romain Rolland und Stefan Zweig]\nYiwei mosheng nüzi de laixin [Der Brief einer Unbekannten]\nGu [Der Amokläufer]\nQimiao zhi ye [Phantastische Nacht]\nZuori de shijie [Die Welt von Gestern]\nJueming shu [Zweig’s “Declaração” / Suicide note]\nYige nüren de yishengzhong de ershisi xiaoshi [Vierundzwanzig Stunden aus dem Leben einer Frau]\nYese menglong [Geschichte in der Dämmerung]\nLeipolaila [Leporella]\nMalai kuangren [Der Amokläufer]\nYuexia xiao xiang [Die Mondscheingasse]\nBaoshou buzhu de mimi [Brennendes Geheimnis]\nQing wang [Sommernovellette]\nHende’er de fuhuo [Georg Friedrich Händels Auferstehung]\nQi yü [Phantastische Nacht]\nXiatian de gushi [Sommernovellette]\nZouxiang tianguo [Die Flucht zu Gott]\nMali wenchuan de aige [Die Marienbader Elegie]\nKanbujian de shougcang [Die unsichtbare Sammlung]\nFugui meng [Rausch der Verwandlung]\nJiating nü jiaoshi [Die Gouvernante]\nYiye tiancai [Das Genie einer Nacht]\n\nC. Chronology\n\nWen Qi. “Ciweige shengping he zhuzuo nianbiao [Chronology of Zweig’s life and works]”, pp. 305-307",
      "sourceBlobId": 4
