      "bibliographicCitation": "Volumes / See also: Chess\n\n[1944]: The Viking Press, New York\n\nThe Royal Game [Schachnovelle]. Translated by Benjamin W. Huebsch. 17p. This is a reprint of: \"The Royal Game\" [Schachnovelle. Translated by Benjamin W. Huebsch] in Woman's Home Companion [Springfield, Ohio], LXXI:3 [7 March 1944], pp. 22-23, 96-98, 100, 106-111, 114-115\n\n[1949]: Greenberg Publishing Company, New York\n\n\"The Royal Game\" [Schachnovelle. Translated by Benjamin W. Huebsch] in The Chess Reader. The Royal Game in World Literature [Compiled by Jerome Salzmann], pp. 29-359\n\n[1966]: MD Publications, Inc., New York\n\n\"The Royal Game\" [Schachnovelle. Translated by Benjamin W. Huebsch] in MD. Medical Newsmagazine [New York], 10:12 [December 1966], pp. 224-248. Contains 3 ilustrations\n\n[1969]: Eihosha Ltd., Tokyo\n\nThe Royal Game [Schachnovelle]. Translated by Benjamin W. Huebsch. Edited with an introduction and notes in Japanese by Hisazumi Tagiri. iv/91p. [Kaleidoscope Two]\n\n[1985]: Reader's Digest Association, Pleasantville, New York\n\n\"The Royal Game\" [Schachnovelle. Translated by Jill Sutcliffe] in Ten of the Best. A Reader's Digest Collection of Great short Novels. Edited by Herbert Lieberman. 2 illustrations by Erhard Göttlicher. 707p. Biographical sketch, p. 604. \"The Royal Game\", pp. (357)-408\n\n[2001]: Pushkin Press, London\n\nThe Royal Game [Schachnovelle]. Translated by Benjamin W. Huebsch. 79p. Cover illustration by André\n\nReview: Mark Thwaite. \"'Royal Game' by Stefan Zweig\" in ReadySteadyBook - for literature, 8 December 2004. See: http://www.readysteadybook.com/BookReview.aspx?isbn=1901285111\n\nIndividual Stories\n\n\"The Royal Game\" [Schachnovelle] in:\n\nC. H.\nChessworld [New York], 1:2 [March/April 1964], pp. (54)-79. Contains 4 illustrations by Patrick O'Brien\nThe Collected Novellas of Stefan Zweig [2015], No. 2, pp. 91-150 [Here entitled \"A Chess Story\"]\nThe Philadelphia Inquirer [Philadelphia], Sunday, 14 November 1948, Literary Section [8p.]\nKaleidoscope Two [1951] [6], pp. 131-188\nThe Royal Game [2001]\nThe Royal Game * Amok * Letter from an Unknown Woman [1944], No. 1, pp. (7)-71 / [1944] Editions for the Armed Services, No. 1, pp. 5-83\nThe Royal Game and Other Stories [2000], No. 3, pp. 1-41\nThe Royal Game * Letter from an Unknown Woman * Amok [1944], No. 1, pp. 5-59\nTwenty-four Hours in the Life of a Woman * The Royal Game [2006], No. 2, pp. (77)-133 \n\nA few Excerpts\n\n[1973]\n\n\"The Royal Game\" [Schachnovelle. Translated by Benjamin Huebsch] in C. H. O'D. Alexander. A Book of Chess. Designed and edited by Derek Birdsall. London: Hutchinson & Company Publishers / New York: Harper & Row Publisher, 1973, pp. 147-150. Introductory remarks by C. H. O'D. Alexander, p. 147. 1 illustration, p. 148\n\n[1983]\n\n\"The Royal Game\" [Schachnovelle. Translated by Benjamin Huebsch] in W. R. Hartston & P. C. Wason. The Psychology of Chess. London: Batsford Publisher, 1983, pp. 22-23. 2nd imprint: New York: Facts on File, Inc., 1984, pp. 22-23\n\n[1993]\n\n\"The Royal Game\" [Schachnnovelle. Translated by Jill Sutcliffe] in The 64-Square Looking Glass. The Great Game of Chess in World Literature. Edited by Burt Hochberg. New York: Random House Publishing Company, 1993, pp. 57-65. Introductory remarks by Burt Honberg",
