      "bibliographicCitation": "Stefan Zweig, 1881-1942. Centenary Symposium [10 December 1981]. This symposium was held at the Institute of Germanic Studies, 29 Russell Square, London WC18 5DP, under the auspices of the Institute of Germanic Studies and the Austrian Institute\n\nSession 1 [Chairman: Professor Sir Ernst Gombrich]\n\nOtto Kolleritsch [Hochschule für Musik, Graz]: \"Richard Strauss und Stefan Zweig - Zur Problemlosigkeit einer künstlerischen Zusammenarbeit\"\n\nSession 2 [Chairman: Professor J. P. Stern. Honorary Director, Institute of Germanic Studies, University of London]\n\nJ. D. A. Warren [Oxford Polytechnic]: \"Stefan Zweig, Jeremias and the Anti-War Drama of the First World War\"\nDavid Turner [University of Hull]: \"Imagery and the Image of Man in Stefan Zweig’s Novellen\"\nSylvia M. Patsch [Universität Innsbruck]: \"Stefan Zweig und Ben Jonson\"",
