      "bibliographicCitation": "[2009]: Armando Dadò Editore, Locarno\n\nSull'orlo dell'abisso. Diario di guerra in Svizzera [On the Edge of the Abyss. Diary of the War in Switzerland]. Translated and edited with an introduction by Mattia Mantovani. Cover design: Salvador Dalí's Le devenir géologique (1933). Pagination make-up by Katya Bianda. 274/(2)p. [Series: I cristalli. Helvetia nobilis, 22]\n\nContents:\n\nLa cittadella assediata [Mattia Mantovani], pp. 5-26\n\nSull'orlo dell'abisso\n\nDiario di guerra in Svizzera [13 novembre 1917 - febbraio 1918], pp. (27)-93 [Source: Stefan Zweig. Tagebücher. Edited by Knut Beck. Frankfurt am Main: S. Fischer Verlag, 1988, pp. 255-307]\nDiario di guerra in Svizzera [20 settembre - 13 novembre 1918], pp. (95)-131 [Source: Stefan Zweig. Tagebücher', 1988, pp. 309-339]\nLettere dalla Svizzera [30 letters by Zweig to various friends, 17 November 1917 - 23 March 1919], pp. (131)-237 [Source: Stefan Zweig. Briefe 1914-1919. Edited by Knut Beck, Jeffrey B. Berlin, and Natascha Weschenbach-Feggeler. Frankfurt am Main: S. Fischer Verlag, 1998, pp. 168-271. The letters are listed below\n\nApendice [Appendixes]\n\nLa Svizzera il soccorso dell'Europa (1918) [Die Schweiz als Hilfsland Europa], pp. 241-245 [Source: Stefan Zweig. Auf Reisen. Edited by Knut Beck. Frankfurt am Main: S. Fischer Verlag, 2004, pp. 221-225]\nNecrologio per un hotel (1918) [Nekrolog auf ein Hotel], pp. 247-252 [Source: Auf Reisen, 2004, pp. 226-231]\nTitoli originali e fonti [Original titles and sources], p. 253\nTavola cronologica [Chronology of Zweig's life and works], pp. 255-264\nIndici [Indexes assembled by Lucia Soncin], pp. (265)-274: [1]. Indice dei nomi di persona [Index of Names], pp. 267-272. [B]. Indice dei nomi di luogo [Index of Places], pp. 273-274\nIndice [Table of Contents], p. (275)\n\nLettere dalla Svizzera\n\nAuernheimer, Raoul, 18 June 1918, pp. 192-195 [No. 17]\nBab, Julius, 20 February 1918, pp. 177-178 [No. 12]\nBloch, Jean-Richard, 23 March 1919, pp. 235-237 [No. 30]\nBuber, Martin, Undated, ca. February 1918, pp. 174-176 [No. 11]\nFleischer, Victor, 29 July 1918, pp. 202-203 [No. 20]\nFleischer, Victor, 6 August 1918, pp. 209-210 [No. 22]\nFleicher, Victor, 13 October 1918, pp. 215-217 [No. 25]\nHesse, Hermann, 2 May 1918, pp. 190-191 [No. 16]\nLudwig, Emil, 29 April 1918, pp. 188-189 [No. 15]\nNeue Freie Presse [Wien], 23 December 1917, pp. 155-158 [No. 6]\nRolland, Romain, 17 November 1917, pp. 135-137 [No. 1]\nRolland, Romain, 29 November 1917, pp. 142-144 [No. 3]\nRolland, Romain, 9 December 1917, pp. 145-151 [No. 4]\nRolland, Romain, 16 December 1917, pp. 152-154 [No. 5]\nRolland, Romain, 23 December 1917, pp. 159-161 [No. 7]\nRolland, Romain, 3 January 1918, pp. 162-164 [No. 8]\nRolland, Romain, 21 January 1918, pp. 165-170 [No. 9]\nRolland, Romain, 30 January 1918, pp. 171-173 [No. 10]\nRolland, Romain, 3 March 1918, pp. 179-183 [No. 13]\nRolland, Romain, 23 March 1918, pp. 184-187 [No. 14]\nRolland, Romain, 21 June 1918, pp. 196-198 [No. 18]\nRolland, Romain, 31 July 1918, pp. 204-208 [No. 21]\nRolland, Romain, 17 September 1918, pp. 213-214 [No. 24]\nRolland, Romain, 21 October 1918, pp. 218-221 [No. 26]\nRolland, Romain, 10 December 1918, pp. 222-224 [No. 27]\nRolland, Romain, 18 December 1918, pp. 225-229 [No. 28]\nRolland, Romain, Undated [Presumably ca. end of December 1918], pp. 230-234 [No. 29]\nSeelig, Carl, 11 September 1918, pp. 211-212 [No. 23]\nTestamento, Villeneuve, 28 November 1917, pp. 138-141 [No.2]. Zweig's attitude toward the First World War and his personal military service is clearly expressed in this \"Testament\". See: Stefan Zweig. Briefe 1914-1919. Edited by Knut Beck, Jeffrey B. Berlin, and Natascha Weschenbach-Feggeler. Frankfurt am Main: S. Fischer Verlag, 1998, pp. 173-179. Notes, pp. 458-459\nWinternitz, Friderike Maria von, ca. 19 July 1918, pp. 199-201 [No. 19]",
