      "bibliographicCitation": "Edited by Hans H. Schulte and Gerald Chapple. New York: Peter Lang Publishing Inc., 2009\n\nZweig references\n\n[1]. Klaus Zeyringer. \"Prologue: Austrian Literature - A Concept\" [Translated from the German by Matthew Pollard], pp. (5)-33. Zweig, p. 6\n\n[2]. Karl Wagner. \"Austrian Literature in the Age of Liberalism\", pp. (37)-56. Zweig, pp. 38, 40, 41, 55 [Notes 2, 6]\n\n[3]. Karl Müller. \"The Two Faces of Austria between the World Wars\" [Translated from the German by Karin Doerr], pp. (57)-86. Zweig, pp. 59, 70-71, 73, 78, 82 [Note 8], 84 [Note 39]\n\n[4]. Paul Michael Lützeler. \"Literature by Austrians in Exile from 1933 to 1945\" [Translated from the German by John L. Plews], pp. (87)-106. Zweig, pp. 91, 92, 93, 98-99, 101, 102 [Note 6], 103 [Notes 23-26, 29, 33], 105 [Notes 66-71]\n\n[5. Harry Zohn. \"Epilogue: I am from Vienna\" [Translated from the German by Paul Malone], pp. (257)-266. Zweig, pp. 260, 262\n\n[6].Index of Names, pp. (269)-272, Zweig, p. 272. Correct p. 77 to read p. 78",
