      "bibliographicCitation": "[1983]: Camden House, Columbia, SC\n\nThe Corresppondence of Stefan Zweig with Raoul Auernheimer and Richard Beer-Hofmann. Edited with an introduction and notes by Donald G. Daviau and Jorun B. Johns [Correspondence with Raoul Auernheimer]. Edited with commentaries and notes by Jeffrey B. Berlin [Correspondence with Richard Beer-Hofmann]. (xiv)/273p. Frontispiece photograph of Stefan Zweig. Photograph of Raoul Auernheimer, opposite p, (1). Photograph of Richard Beer-Hofmann, opposite p. 112. Photograph of Raoul and Irene Auernheimer in California, opposite p. 113. Photograph of Richard Beer-Hofmann, opposite pp. (167). Photograph of Ben Huebsch and Stefan Zweig, opposite p. 188. In-between pp. 186-177, photographs of Richard Beer-Hofmann’s letter to Zweig, 8 May 1925 and Zweig to Beer-Hofmann, 1 December 1931 [Studies in German Literature, Linguistics and Culture, 20]\n\nContents\n\nPreface: The Correspondence of Stefan Zweig with Raoul Auernheimer and Richard Beer-Hofmann, pp. (vii)-viii\nAcknowledgements, pp. (ix)-x\n \n\nPart I: The Correspondence of Stefan Zweig with Raoul Auernheimer, pp. (35)-129. Notes, pp. 129-163\n\nIntroduction, pp. (1)-33\nAuernheimer to Zweig, 110 letters and cards, 12 November 1905-4 November 1939\nZweig to Auernheimer, 77 letters and cards, (Prior to 19 February 1911)-(April/May 1941)\n\nPart II: The Correspondence of Stefan Zweig with Richard Beer-Hofmann with Unpublished Letters to Sol Liptzin and Ben Huebsch, pp. (165)-205. Notes, pp. 206-233\n\nBeer-Hofmann to Zweig, 4 letters, 3 notes, 3 September 1917, 8 May 1925, July 1926, 6 October 1933, 19 December 1933, 22 December 1935, 4 March 1935. Opposite p. 176, facsimile of the letter from Beer-Hofmann to Zweig, 8 May 1925\nZweig to Beer-Hofmann, 3 letters, 3 notes, 2 postcards, April 1926, 1 December 1931, 1932, 30 December 1933, 11 July 1940, (21 January 1941), (24 March 1941), (April 1941?) .Opposite p. 177, facsimile of the letter from Zweig to Beer-Hofmann, 1 December 1931 \n\nThis section also contains the following letters, notes or excerpts thereof: \n\nZweig to Ben Huebsch, 2 letters, 19 December 1933, 30 December 1933\nHuebsch to Zweig, 1 letter, 16 January 1934\nZweig to Sol Liptzin, 2 letters, 30 June 1930, 13 February 1936\nBeer-Hofmann to Ben Huebsch, 2 letters, 1 postcard, 3 October 1933, 23 July 1934, 12 August 1934\nBeer-Hofmann to Liptzin, 2 letters, 13 November 1933, 12 March 1934\nLiptzin to Beer-Hofmann, 1 letter, 2 January 1934\nBeer-Hofmann to Alfred Miller, 1 letter, 19 December 1933\nBeer-Hofmann to Herbert Steiner, 1 note, 9 July 1940\nHerbert Steiner to Beer-Hofmann, 1 note, 11 [12?] July 1940\nBeer-Hofmann to Sam Wachtell, 1 letter, 20 October 1939\nBeer-Hofmann to Hermann Weigand, 1 letter, 16 April 1944\nKonrad Maril [S. Fischer Verlag] to Beer-Hofmann, 1 letter, 12 December 1933\nGertrud Rung to Beer-Hofmann, 1 letter, 15 May 1925\nSam Wachtell to Erich Kahler, 1 letter, 31 October 1939\nFriderike Maria Zweig to Paula Beer-Hofmann, 1 note, no date\nZweig to Gisella Selden-Goth, Spring 1940\nArthur Schnitzler, 1 letter [Excerpt], 4 November 1929. See Note 69, pp. 217-218\n\nSelect Bibliography\n\nStefan Zweig, pp. 236-239\nRaoul Auernheimer, pp. 239-245\nRichard Beer-Hofmann, pp. 245-246\nSecondary Literature, pp. 246-261",
      "sourceBlobId": 3
