      "bibliographicCitation": "English:\n\nThe Origins of Totalitarianism. 520p. New York: Meridian Books, 1958. Bibliography, pp. 483-507. Quotations from Stefan Zweig, pp. 50, 52, 332\n\n\"Portrait of a Period\" in The Menorah Journal [New York], 31:3 [October 1943], pp. 307-314. A critical review of Zweig's autobiography The World of Yesterday. An Autobiography. Translated by Benjamin Huebsch and Helmut Ripperger. London: Cassell / New York: The Viking Press, 1943\n\nReprinted in:\n\nThe Jew as Pariah. Jewish Identity and Politics in the Modern Age. By Hannah Arendt. Edited by Ron H. Feldman. New York: Grove Press, 1978, pp. 112-121. See German below: \"Juden in der Welt von Gestern\" and Das große Schweigen\n\nFrench:\n\n\"Les Juifs dans le monde d'hier\" in La Tradition cachée. Le juif comme paria. By Hannah Arendt. Translated by Sylvie Courtine-Denamy. Paris: Christian Bourgois Éditeur, 1987, pp. 77-95. Reprinted: Paris: Union générale d'édition, 1997; London: Cox & Wyman, 1993; Paris: Christian Bourgois Éditeur, 2000\n\nGerman:\n\n“Juden in der Welt von gestern. Anläßlich Stefan Zweig, The World of Yesterday. An Autobiography” in Sechs Essays. By Hannah Arendt. Heidelberg: Lambert Schneider Verlag, 1948, pp. 112-127\n\nReprinted in:\n\nDie verborgene Tradition. Acht Essays. By Hannah Arendt. Frankfurt am Main: Suhrkamp Verlag, 1976, pp. 74-(87) [suhrkamp taschenbuch, 303]\n\nExcerpts in:\n\nStefan Zweig. Bilder, Texte, Dokumente [1993], p. 195 / No. XVII E 1\nStefan Zweig - Triumph und Tragik. Aufsätze, Tagebuchnotizen, Briefe [1992], No. 66, pp. 158-161",
      "sourceBlobId": 5
    },
