        "Secondary Literature / Authors (German)"
      ],
      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "Gedächtnisfeier für Stefan Zweig zum 62. Geburtstage am 25.(sic) 11. 1943. Manuscript. 17 folios. Berthold Auerbach Collection, University of London School of Advanced Study, Institute of Germanic & Romance Studies. A speech/essay by Auerbach, written the year following Stefan Zweig’s death in exile in Brazil. It presents a synopsis of Zweig’s life and work, drawing attention to the influence of Sigmund Freud on both",
      "sourceBlobId": 0
    },
