      ],
      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "The Austrian Mind. An Intellectual and Social History, 1848-1938. Berkeley/Los Angeles/London: University of California Press, 1972 [Reprinted 1976, 1983]. Zweig references, pp. 27 [Note 30, p. 409], 30-31, 51, 118 [Note 8, p. 421], 122, 166 [Note 5, p. 430], 179 [Note 37, p. 433], 212, 358 [Note 2, p. 466], 402, 484, Index p. 515\n\nFrench translation\n\n L'Esprit viennois. Une histoire intellectuelle et sociale 1848-1938. Translated by Pierre-Emmanuel Dauzat. XVII/643p. Paris: Presses Universitraires de France, 1991 [Quadrige, 124]. Zweig references, pp. 28 [Note 34, p. 475], 32-33 [Note 2, p. 477], 55, 130 [Note 8, p. 496], 135, 138 [Note 33, p. 499], 204 [Note 6, p. 520], 218 [Note 46, pp. 525-526], 255, 417 [Note 3, p. 576. See also Note 1], 466, 479 [Note 2], 512 [Note 8], 605, 643",
