      "bibliographicCitation": "“Stefan Zweigs Tod” [Lecture, Los Angeles, 1942] in Stefan Zweig. Sein Leben - Sein Werk [1949], No. 14, pp. 177-187\n\nReprinted in\n\nDeutsche Abschiede. Edited with an afterword by Gerhard Hay. München: Winkler Verlag, (1984), pp. 323-329. Further Zweig references, pp. 460, 477, 493, 495\nDer große Europäer Stefan Zweig [1956], No. 32, pp. 269-282\nDer große Europäer Stefan Zweig [1960], No. 33, pp. 270-283\nDer große Europäer Stefan Zweig [1981], No. 32, pp. 148-155\nÖsterreichische Schriftsteller im Exil. Texte. Edited by Sylvia Maria Patsch. Wien/München: Christian Brandstätter Verlag, (1986), pp. 49-56\nStefan Zweig. Im Zeugnis seiner Freunde [1968], No. 37, pp. 208-216\nUnsterblicher Genius. Deutsche Dichter im Gedenken ihrer Freunde. Edited by Paul Schneider. Ebenhausen bei München: Hartfried Voss Verlag, 1959, pp. 317-323\n\nEnglish version\n\n“Stefan Zweig’s Death” in Stefan Zweig. A Tribute to His Life and Work [1951], No. 13, pp. 138-146\n\nSee\n\nEnderlin, Renate. Stefan Zweig in einem biographischen Essay Franz Werfels: “Stefan Zweigs Tod”\nFranz Werfel Archives, University of California, Los Angeles, Department of Special Collections, 120 Lawrence Clark Powell Library, Los Angeles, CA 90024. The archives contain the original 6-page autograph version of Werfel’s lecture and the 8-page typescript thereof. A copy, handwritten by Werfel, is also located the Friderike Maria Zweig Archives, Reed Library, State University of New York, Fredonia, NY 14063. The archives also contain one letter concerning Franz Werfel and three telegrams concerning his death",
