      "bibliographicCitation": "[2010/2011/2012]: Transaction Publishers, New Brunswick, NJ and London, England\n\nMaster Builders of the Spirit [Baumeister der Welt]. Translated by Eden and Cedar Paul. With a new introduction by Laurence Mintz. 3 vols. The new introduction is reprinted in each of the three volumes. Originally published as Master Builders. A Typology of the Spirit in 1930 by the Viking Press, New York. See: Baumeister der Welt\n\nVol. 1. Balzac, Dickens, Dostoevsky. Three Masters. liii/(1)-238p. 2010\n\nContents:\n\nAuthor's Note [Stefan Zweig], p. (vii)\nIntroduction to the Transaction Edition [Laurence Mintz], pp. ix-l\nIntroduction [Stefan Zweig. Salzburg, 1919], pp. li-liii\nBalzac, pp. (1)-48\nDickens, pp. (49)-95\nDostoeffsky, pp. (97)-238\n\nVol. 2. Hölderlin, Kleist and Nietzsche. The Struggle with the Daemon. l/241-530p. 2011\n\nContents:\n\nIntroduction to the Transaction Edition [Laurence Mintz], pp. ix-l\nIntroduction [Stefan Zweig], pp. 241-256\nHölderlin, pp. (257)-367\nKleist, pp. (369)-440\nNietzsche, pp. (441)-530\n\nVol. 3. Casanova, Stendhal, Tolstoy. Adepts in Self-Portraiture. xlv/533-905p. 2012\n\nContents:\n\nIntroduction to the Transaction Edition [Laurence Mintz], pp. vii-xlv\nIntroduction [Stefan Zweig, Salzburg, Easter 1928], pp. 533-547\nCasanova, pp. (549)-649\nStendhal, pp. (651)-755\nTolstoy, pp. (757)-905",
