      "mainCategory": "Correspondence",
      "bibliographicCitation": "[2013]: Fischer Taschenbuch Verlag, Frankfurt am Main\n\n'Ich wunschte, dass ich Ihnen Ihnen ein wenig fehlte'. Briefe an Lotte Zweig 1934-1940. Edited with introductions, copious notes, translations, and an appendix by Oliver Matuschek. 367p. Illustrated with 68 photographs [48 of people, 20 of places and documents] [Fischer Klassik. Hardcover]\n\nTeil I: 1 May 1934 - 14 June 1935. Introduction, pp. 9-15. Letters, pp. 15-135\n\n1934\n\nStefan Zweig to Lotte Altmann, 12 letters and 4 postcards, 1 May 1934 - 9 September 1934\nFriderike Maria Zweig to Lotte Altmann, 1 letter, (mid-July 1934)\nLotte Altmann to Manfred Altmann [her brother], 1 postcard, 31 December 1934\n\n1935\n\nLotte Altmann to Stefan Zweig, 1 letter, (8 January 1935)\nStefan Zweig to Lotte Altmann, 38 letters and 3 postcards, 6 January 1935 - 24 December 1935\nStefan Zweig to the French Consulate in London, 1 letter, 14 June 1935\n\nTeil II: 30 April 1936 - 9 November 1938. Introduction, pp. 139-142. Letters, pp. 143-227\n\n1936\n\nStefan Zweig to Friderike Maria Zweig, 4 letters, 30 April and (beginning of May) 1936\nStefan Zweig to Lotte Altmann, 14 letters, 20 June 1936 - 20 December 1936\n\n1937: Introduction, pp. 171-173\n\nStefan Zweig to Friderike Maria Zweig, 1 letter, (ca. beginning of 1937)\nFriderike Maria Zweig to Stefan Zweig, 2 letters, 21 March and 30 July 1937\nJohann Thalhuber [Zweig's servant in Salzburg] to Stefan Zweig, 1 letter, (ca. March 1937)\nStefan Zweig to Alix von Winternitz [Friderike Maria's daughter], 1 letter, 29 July 1937\nAlfred Zweig [Zweig's brother] to Stefan Zweig, 2 letters, 10 and 11 September 1937\nStefan Zweig to Lotte Altmann, 7 letters and 5 postcards, (ca. May 1937) - 26 November 1937\n\n1938: Introduction , pp. 217-224\n\nStefan Zweig to Lotte Altmann, 1 postcard, 8 November 1938 and 1 letter, 9 November 1938\n\nTeil III: 20 and 21 December - 25 June 1940. Introduction, pp. 231-233. Letters, pp. 233-316\n\n1938\n\nLotte Altmanm to Eva Altmann [Lotte's niece], 1 letter, 20/21 December 1938. On-board the Normandie en route to New York. Contains a list of the cities in which Stefan Zweig was to lecture, 9 January to 26 February\n\n1939: Introduction, pp. 235-236\n\nStefan Zweig to Hannah Altmann [Lotte's sister-in-law], 10 letters, (13 January 1939) - 15 December 1939\nStefan and Lotte Zweig to Hannah Altmann, 6 letters, 23 September 1939 - 19 December 1939\nLotte Zweig to Hannah Altmann, 1 letter, (11 September 1939)\nStefan Zweig to Lotte Zweig and Hannah Altmann, 1 letter, (ca. 15 September 1939)\nEva Altmann and Stefan Zweig to Hannah Altmann, 1 letter, 2 December 1939\n\n1940: Introduction, pp. 238-246 and Introductory remarks, p. 282\n\nStefan and Lotte Zweig to Hannah Altmann, 1 letter, (ca. beginning of January 1940)\nStefan Zweig and others to Hannah Zweig, 1 letter, 29 January 1940\nStefan Zweig to Hannah Altmann, 3 letters and 1 postcard, (ca. 19 February 1940) - 4 April 1940\nStefan and Lotte Zweig to Hannah and Manfred Altmann, 1 letter, (after 15 March 1940)\nStefan Zweig to Lotte Zweig, 11 letters, 10 April - (27 April) 1940\nLotte Altmann [=Zweig] to Eva Altmann and Ursula Mayer (Eva's cousin), 1 letter, (24 June 1940)\nStefan Zweig to Eva Altmann and Ursula Mayer, 1 letter, (24 June 1940)\nStefan Zweig and Lotte to Martha Kahn [Hannah's sister], 1 letter, 25 June 1940\n\nAnhang\n\nStefan Zweig und Lotte Altmann - Annäherung an eine Annäherung, pp. 321-329\nListe der Dokumente mit Übertragungen der fremdsprachigen Texte, pp. 330-351\nBiographische Angaben zu den wichtigsten erwähnten Familienmitgliedern, pp. 352-356\nVerzeichnis der Quellen und Siglen, pp. 357-358\nBenutzte und weiterführende Literatur, pp. 359-362\nAbbildungsnachweise, p. 363\nVerzeichnis der erwähnten Personen, pp. 364-367\n\nReviews\n\n[1]. Graebner, Klaus. \"Wenn Pazifisten Krieg fuehren\" in Fraenkischer Tag [Bamberg], 27/28 July 2013\n\n[2]. Isenschmid, Andreas. \" Ungeistige Lebensform in Die Zeit'' [Hamburg], 1 August 2013, No. 32, p. 41\n\n[3]. Pfohlmann, Oliver. \"'London' statt 'Salzburg'. Friederikes langer Schatten - eine Edition von Stefan Zweigs Briefen an seine zweite Frau Lotte\" in Neue Zürcher Zeitung [Zürich], Internationale Ausgabe, 10 August 2013, No. 183, p. 26\n\n[4]. Weidermann, Volker. \"Der schwere Kampf für eine schöne Sache. Wie sich der Meister der psychologischen Novelle in seinen letzten Jahren im eigenen Seelenleben verlief: Die Briefe Stefan Zweigs an seine Frau Lotte\" in Frankfurter Allgemeine Zeitung [Frankfurt am Main], No. 108 [11 May 2013], p. 33. Contains two photographs",
      "sourceBlobId": 3
