        "klawiter:CorrespondenceEntry"
      ],
      "@id": "klawiter:entry/2708",
      "entryType": "correspondence",
      "sourcePageId": 2708,
      "pageNamespace": 0,
      "name": {
        "@value": "The Stols-Archives of the Bibliotheek Zuid-Kennemerland, Haarlem, Holldand contain 22 letters pertaining to Stefan Zweig:",
        "@language": "de"
      },
      "sourceTextId": 14990,
      "author": {
        "@id": "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q78491",
        "@type": "schema:Person",
        "name": "Stefan Zweig"
      },
      "datePublished": "1932",
      "allYears": [
        1925,
        1932,
        1933,
        1934,
        1937,
        1938,
        1959
      ],
      "timePeriod": "lifetime",
      "publisher": {
        "@id": "klawiter:publisher/Herbert%20Reichner%20Verlag",
        "@type": "schema:Organization",
        "name": "Herbert Reichner Verlag"
      },
      "locationCreated": {
        "@id": "klawiter:place/Wien",
        "@type": "schema:Place",
        "name": "Wien",
        "sameAs": "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1741"
      },
      "allLocations": [
        "Wien",
        "London",
        "Salzburg"
      ],
      "inLanguage": "de",
      "languageName": "German",
      "categories": [
        "Correspondence / Individual Letters (German)"
      ],
      "mainCategory": "Correspondence",
      "bibliographicCitation": "The Stols-Archives of the Bibliotheek Zuid-Kennemerland, Haarlem, Holldand contain 22 letters pertaining to Stefan Zweig:\n\nHerbert Reichner [Herbert Reichner Verlag, Wien] to the publisher A. A. M. Stols, 8 December 1932. Concerning a typographical printing of Zweig's novella \"Die unsichtbare Sammlung\" to be added as a supplement to Philobiblon. Eine Zeitschrift für Bücherliebhaber [Reichner Verlag, Wien]. A revised version of this story did indeed appear as a 15-page supplement to the Philobiblon [Wien], 6:9 [November 1933]. The original version of \"Die unsichtbare Sammlung\" appeared in the Neue Freie Press [Wien], 31 May 1925, pp. 2-7\nStefan Zweig to A. A. M. Stols, 13 letters, 20 April 1933-28 October 1937. Two of these letters were sent by Zweig's secretary [28 April 1933 and 23 October 1937]. There is also one telegram, 23 November 1934: \"Sendet bucher nicht London sondern Salzburg. Zweig\" \nA. A. M. Stols to Stefan Zweig, 6 letters, 24 May 1934-25 January 1938. There is also a letter from Stols to the Amsterdamsche Bank, 26 October 1937, requesting that 77.43 florins be sent to Zweig as a royalty payment for the sale of the Dutch translation of Zweig's Erasmus\nFriderike Maria Zweig to an unnamed recipient, 1 letter, 3 March 1959. The letter, written in French, is a thank you note for the recipient's willingness to send her copies of the Zweig letters in his possession. She also sent the recipient a copy of a letter by Erich Fitzbauer announcing the formation of the Stefan Zweig Gesellschaft, Wien VIII, Piaristengasse 46/17. Erich Fitzbauer was the president of the Stefan Zweig Gesellschaft, Friderike Maria Zweig was the honorary president of the society",
      "sourceBlobId": 1
    },
