      "bibliographicCitation": "[1987]: Insel Verlag, Frankfurt am Main\n\nRainer Maria Rilke und Stefan Zweig in Briefen und Dokumenten. Edited with a foreword, explanatory comments, and annotations by Donald A. Prater. 179/(1)p. Illustrated with 6 photographs [Stefan Zweig, Rainer Maria Rilke, Franz Karl Ginzkey, Emile Verhaeren, and Romain Rolland]\n\nContents:\n\nVorwort [Donald A. Prater], pp. 7-(12). Annotations: Nos. 1-17, p. 153\n\n1906-1909: \n\n1906-1909: \"Die volle Herzlichkeit seines Wesens\", pp. 15-(49). Annotations: Nos. 1-43, pp. 154-157. Explanatory comments, p. 15. The comments contain an excerpt from a letter by Zweig to Ellen Key, 9 February 1906. Annotation: No. 1, p. 154\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, (ca. 2 March 1906), pp. 15-16. Annotations: Nos. 2-4, p. 154\nExplanatory comments, pp. 16-17. Annotations: Nos. 5-6, p. 154. The comments contain an excerpt from a letter by Zweig to Ellen Key, 15 April 1906, p. 17. Annotation: No. 5, p. 154\nStefan Zweig. \"Verse eines Gottsuchers\", pp. 17-21. Explanatory comments, p. 21. Annotations: No. 7, p. 154. This is a review of Rilke's volume Das Stundenbuch: Vom mönchischen Leben / Von der Pilgerschaft / Von der Armuth und vom Tode. Leipzig: Insel- Verlag, 1905. Reprinted in: Begegnungen mit Büchern. Aufsätze und Einleitungen aus den Jahren 1902-1939 [Frankfurt am Main, 1983], No. 10, pp. 80-84\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, (ca. December 1906), p. 21. Explanatory comments, p. 22. Annotations, Nos. 8-9, p. 154\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, Abend vor Dreikönig (Evening before the Epiphany, 5 January) 1907, pp. 22-23. Annotations: Nos. 10-11, p. 154\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, 14 February 1907, pp. 23-26. Explanatory comments, p. 23. Annotations: Nos. 12-18, pp. 154-155\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, 4 March 1907, pp. 26-28. Annotation: No. 19, p. 155\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, 11 March 1907, pp. 28-32. Annotations: Nos. 20-22, p. 155\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, (End of July 1907), p. 33. Annotation: No. 23, p. 155\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, 3 August 1907, pp. 34-35. Annotations: Nos. 24-26, pp. 155-156\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, 5 August 1907, pp. 36-39. Annotations: Nos. 27-29, p. 156\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, 11 August 1907, pp. 39-40. Annotation, No. 30, p. 156. Explanatory comments, p. 41. Annotations: Nos. 31-33, pp. 156-157\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, 8 September 1908, pp. 41-42. Annotations: Nos 34-35, p. 157\nStefan Zweig. \"Rilkes 'Neue Gedichte'\", pp. 43-46. Explanatory comment, p. 43. Annotation: Nos. 36-37, p. 157. This is a review of Rilke's Neue Gedichte. Leipzig: Insel-Verlag, 1907. The review was first published in Das literarische Echo [Berlin], 11:6 [15 December 1908], cols. 416-418. Reprinted in: Begegnungen mit Büchern. Aufsätze und Einleitungen aus den Jahren 1902-1939 [Frankfurt am Main, 1983], No. 11, pp. 85-(89)\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, (14 March 1909), p. 47. Explanatory comment, p. 47. Annotations: No. 38, p. 157\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, (ca. March or April 1909], pp. 47-48. Explanatory comments, p. 48. Annotations: Nos. 39-40, p. 157. The Explanatory comments contain an excerpt from a letter by Zweig to Paul Zech, 15 June 1910\nRilke to Anton Kippenberg, 1 letter [an excerpt], 7 December 1911, pp. 48-49. Annotation: No. 41, p. 157\nZweig to Emile Verhaeren, 1 letter [an excerpt], (ca. 20 December 1911), p. (49). Annotations: Nos. 42-43, p. 157\n\n1910-1914:\n\n1910-1914: \"Das Milde und das Mönchische in ihm kontrastiert so erhaben mit der Strenge seiner Aufgabe\", pp. 50-(69). Annotations: Nos. 1-45, pp. 158-162. Explanatory comments, p. 50. Annotation: No. 1, p. 158\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, 12 March 1913, p. 50\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, 13 March 1913, p. 51\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, (14 March 1913), pp. 51-52\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, (15 March 1913), p. 52\nAus Stefan Zweigs Tagebuch [An excerpt from Zweig's Tagebücher [Frankfurt am Main, 1984, pp. 51-52], 17 March (1913), pp. 53-54. Annotations: Nos. 2-4, pp. 158-159\nA photograph of a post card sent by Zweig to Anton Kippenberg. 17 March 1913. Annotation: No. 5, p. 159\nAus Stefan Zweigs Tagebuch [An excerpt from Zweig's Tagebücher [Frankfurt am Main, 1984, pp. 51-52], 18 March (1913), pp. 54-56. Annotations: Nos. 6-11, pp. 159-160\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, 29 March 1913, p. 56\nAus Stefan Zweigs Tagebuch [An excerpt from Zweig's Tagebücher [Frankfurt am Main, 1984], 29 March (1913), p. 57\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, 3 April 1913, p. 57. Annotation: No. 12\n, p. 160\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, (3 April 1913), p. 57. Annotation: No. 13, p. 160\nAus Stefan Zweigs Tagebuch [An excerpt from Zweig's Tagebücher [Frankfurt am Main, 1984, pp. 63-64], 5 April (1913), pp. 58-59. Annotations: Nos. 14-23, p. 160\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, (9 April 1913), p. 59. Annotations: Nos. 24-25, p. 160\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, 11 April 1913, p. 60. Annotation: No. 26, p. 160\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, (ca. 20 April 1913), pp. 60-61. Annotations: Nos. 27-29, p. 161\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, 21 April 1913, p. 61. Annotations: Nos. 30-31, p. 161\nZweig to Paul Zech. 1 letter [An excerpt], (ca. summer 1913), p. 62. Annotation: No. 32, p. 161\nZweig to André Suarès, 1 letter [An excerpt], 14 August 1913, p. 62. Annotations: Nos. 33-34, p. 161\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, 16 September 1913, pp. 62-63. Annotations: Nos. 35-37, pp. 161-162\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, 18 September (1913), pp. 63-64. Annotations: Nos. 38-39, p. 162\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, (ca. 16 March 1914), p. 65. Annotation: No. 40, p. 162\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, (18 April 1914), p. 65. Annotations: Nos. 41- 42, p. 162\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, (18 April 1914), p. 66. Annotation: No. 43, p. 162\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, 4 May 1914,pp. 66-67. Annotation, No. 44, p. 162\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, (ca. 26 May 1914), p. 67\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, 28 May 1914, p. 68. Pages 68-69 contain Rilke's translation of the \"Agnus Dei\"\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, (31 May 1914?), p. (69). Annotation: No. 45, p. 162\n\n1914-1918:\n\n1914-1918: \"Die innere Erstarrung, in der ich lebe\", pp. 70-(102). Annotations, Nos. 1-58, pp. 162-167. Explanatory comments, p. 70\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, 1 May 1915, pp. 70-72. Annotations, Nos. 1-3, pp. 162-163\nExplanatory comments, p. 72. Annotation: No. 4, p. 163\nRilke to Anton Kippenberg, 1 letter [An excerpt], 5 October 1915 [Mailed on 7 October], pp. 73-74\nZweig to Romain Rolland, 1 letter [An excerpt], 30 December 1915, pp. 75-76. Explanatory comment, p. 75. Annotation, No. 5, p. 163\nRomain Rolland to Zweig, 1 letter, 7 January 1916, p. 76\nRomain Rolland to Jacques Copeau, 1 letter [An excerpt], 7 January 1916, p. 77. Annotation: No. 6, p. 163\nAndré Gide to Rolland, 1 letter [An excerpt], 11 January 1916, pp. 77-78\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, 13 January 1916, p. 78. Annotation: No. 7, p. 163\nAus Stefan Zweigs Tagebuch [An excerpt from Zweig's Tagebücher [Frankfurt am Main, 1984, pp. 245-246], 16 (January 1916), p. 79. Annotation: No. 8, p. 163\nZweig to Romain Rolland, 1 letter [An excerpt], 17 January 1916, p. 79\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, 17 January 1916, p. 80\nConcerning Rilke in the military, pp. 80-81. Annotations: Nos. 9-10, p. 163. A quotation from: Siegfried Trebitsch. Chronik eines Lebens. Zürich/Stuttgart/Wien: Artemis-Verlag, 1951, pp. 245-246\nRomain Rolland to Zweig, 1 letter, 17 January 1916, pp. 81-82\nAndré Gide to Romain Rolland, 1 letter [An excerpt], 25 January 1916, pp. 82-83\nAus Stefan Zweigs Tagebuch [An excerpt from Zweig's Tagebücher [Frankfurt am Main, 1984, p. 247], 26 (January 1916), p. 83. Annotations: Nos. 11-12, p. 163\nAus André Gides Tagebuch, 29 January 1916: André Gide. Bericht über die Geschichte der Beschlagnahme von Rilkes Wohnung, pp. 84-85\nRomain Rolland to Zweig, 1 letter [An excerpt], 30 January 1916, p. 86. Annotation: No. 13, p. 163\nExplanatory comments, pp. 86-87. Annotations: Nos. 14-16, p. 163\nAus Stefan Zweigs Tagebuch [An excerpt from Zweig's Tagebücher [Frankfurt am Main, 1984, pp. 249-250 and 253-254], 3 (February 1916) and 21 (February 1916), p. 87. Annotations: Nos. 17-18, pp. 163-164\nZweig to Franz Strunz [Director of the Urania in Vienna], 1 letter [An excerpt], 17 February 1916, p. 88. Annotation: No. 19, p. 164\nRilke to Katharina Kippenberg, 1 letter [An excerpt], 2 March 1916, p. 88. Annotation: No. 20, p. 164\nRilke to Friderike Maria von Winternitz, 1 letter, (7 April 1916), p. 89. Annotation: No. 20, p. 164\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, (22 May 1916?), p. 89. Annotation: No. 23, p. 164\nRilke to Friderike Maria von Winternitz, 1 letter, (27 June 1916?), p. 90. Annotations: Nos. 24-27, p. 164\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, (Summer 1916), pp. 90-91. Annotations: Nos. 28-29, p. 164\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, 23 April 1917, pp. 91-93. Annotations: Nos. 30-34, pp. 164-166\nExplanatory comments, p. 93. Annotations: Nos. 35-38, p. 166\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, 5 September 1917, pp. 94-95. Annotations: Nos. 39-41, p. 166\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, 12 September 1917, p. 95. Annotation: No. 42, p. 167\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, 20 September 1917, p. 96. Annotations: Nos. 43-45, p. 167\nExplanatory comments, p. 97. Annotation: No. 46, p. 167\nAus Stefan Zweigs Tagebuch [An excerpt from Zweig's Tagebücher [Frankfurt am Main, 1984, pp. 265-266], 21 (=20 November 1917), pp. 97-98. Annotations: Nos. 47-50, p. 167\nAus Stefan Zweigs Tagebuch [An excerpt from Zweig's Tagebücher [Frankfurt am Main, 1984, p. 294], 24 (December 1917), p. 98. Annotations: Nos. 51-52, p. 167\nZweig to Rilke, 1 letter, Christmas Eve (24 December 1917), pp. 99-100. Annotation: No. 53, p. 167\nExplanatory comments, p. 100. Annotations: Nos. 54-55, p. 167\nKatharina Kippenberg to Rilke, 1 letter [An excerpt], 31 December 1917, p. 101. Annotation: No. 56, p. 167\nAus Stefan Zweigs Tagebuch [An excerpt from Zweig's Tagebücher [Frankfurt am Main, 1984, p. 299], 6 (January 1918), p. 101. Annotation: No. 57, p. 167\nRilke to Katharina Kippenberg, 1 letter [An excerpt], 14 January 1918, p. (102). Annotation: No. 58, p. 167\n\n1919-1926:\n\n1919-1926: \"Der Brieffeder gewissermaßen unter Aufsicht gestellt\", pp. 103-(107). Annotations: Nos. 1-15, pp. 168-169. Explanatory comments, p. 103. Annotations: Nos 1-3, p. 168\nRilke to Zweig, 1 letter, 9 March 1921, pp. 103-105. Annotations: Nos. 4-6, pp. 168-169\nRilke to Friderike Zweig, 1 letter, 18 March 1921, pp. 105-106. Annotations: Nos. 7-10, p. 169\nExplanatory comments, pp. 106-(107). Annotations: Nos. 11-15, p. 169\n\nNachklang 1927-1942:\n\nNachklang 1927-1942: \"Demütig tritt mein Wort an diese Stunde\", p. 108. Annotation: No. 1, p. 170\nZweig to Anton Kippenberg, 1 letter, (Year's end, 1926/1927), p. 108. Annotation: No. 2, p. 170\nZweig to André Saurès, 1 letter [An excerpt], 4 January 1927, pp. 109-110. Annotations: Nos 3-4, p. 170\nRomain Rolland to Friderike Zweig, 1 letter [An excerpt], 5 January 1927. Annotation: No. 5, p. 170\nStefan Zweig - Raoul Auernheimer Correspondence [Excerpts from three letters. Annotation: No. 6, p. 170]: Zweig to Auernheimer, 5 January 1927, pp. 110-111; Auernheimer to Zweig, 6 January 1927, p. 111; Zweig to Auernheimer, 8 Janaury 1927, pp. 111-112\nZweig to Katharina Kippenberg, 1 letter [An excerpt], 8 January 1927, p. 112. Annotations: Nos. 7-8, p. 170\nZweig to Rudolf Pannwitz, 1 letter [An excerpt], 27 January 1927, pp. 112-113. Annotation: No. 9, p. 170\nStefan Zweig. \"Abschied von Rilke\" [Rede im Rahmen einer Gedächtnisfeier am 20. Februar 1927, gehalten im Staatstheater München], pp. 113-129. Annotation: No. 10, p. 170. Printed in: Begegnungen mit Menschen, Büchern, Städten [Wien/Leipzig/Zürich, 1937], No. 3, pp. (63)-78. A slightly altered version printed in: Das Geheimnis des künstlerischen Schaffens. Essays [Frankfurt am Main, 1984], No. 18, pp. 242-(260)\nZweig to Edmond Jaloux, 2 letters [Excerpts]: 11 March 1928, p. 129. Annotations: Nos. 11-12, pp. 170-171; 7 December (1931?), pp. 129-130\nBen W. Huebsch - Stefan Zweig Correspondence [Excerpts from two letter. Annotations: Nos. 13-15, pp. 171-172]: Huebsch to Zweig, 4 May 1932, pp. 130-131; Zweig to Huebsch, 13 May 1932, p. 131\nStefan Zweig. \"Rainer Maria Rilke\" [Vortrag, gehalten in London bei einem Symposium im 10. Todesjahr Rilkes, 1936], pp. 132-137. Annotation: No. 16, p. 172. Printed in: [1]. Europäisches Erbe [Frankfurt am Main, 1960], No. 21, pp. (244)-250; [Frankfurt am Main, 1981], No. 21, pp. 192-197 [3rd-7th editions, pp. 259-265] and [2].Die Monotonisierung der Welt. Aufsätze und Vorträge [Frankfurt am Main, 1976], No. 18, pp. 211-217\nZweig to Anton Kippenberg, 1 letter [An excerpt], 3 January 1937, pp. 137-138. Annotations: Nos. 17-18, pp. 172-(173)\nStefan Zweig. Die Welt von Gestern. Erinnerungen eines Europäers [An excerpt. 1942 edition, pp. 166-174], pp. 138-145. Annotation: No. 19, p. (173)\nAnlage 1: Zweig to André Saurès, 1 letter [An excerpt], 4 January 1927, pp. 146-147\nAnlage 2: Romain Rolland to Friderike Zweig, 1 letter [An excerpt], 5 January 1927, p. 147\nAnlage 3: Zweig to Edmond Jaloux. 1 letter [An excerpt], 11 March 1928, p. 147\nAnlage 4: Zweig to Edmond Jaloux, 1 letter [An excerpt], 7 December (1931?), p. 148\n\nAnhang:\n\nZur Edition [Donald A. Prater], pp. 151-(152)\nAnmerkungen, pp. 153-(173)\nNamenregister, pp. 174-(177)\nWerkregister: Rilke, p. 178\nWerkregister: Zweig, pp. 179-(180)",
