      "bibliographicCitation": "[2014]: Éditions Albin Michel, Paris\n\nRomain Rolland - Stefan Zweig. Correspondance 1910-1919. Edited with an introduction and annotations by Jean-Yves Brancy. Due to World War I, Stefan Zweig's letters and postcards to Romain Rolland from 6 October 1914 until 14 November 1917 had to be written in German. These were translated into French by Siegrun Barat. 636/(4)p. The book jacket contains a detail from Emil Mayer's photograph \"Vor dem Dritten Kaffeehaus\", Praterhauptallee, Wien (Vienna), 1910\n\nContents:\n\nAvant-propos [Jean-Yves Brancy], pp. 7-(8)\nIntroduction [Jean-Yves Brancy], pp. 9-(21)\nSources, pp. 23-(26)\nAbréviations, p. 27\n\nCorrespondance:\n\n1910. No. 1, pp. 29-(30)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 1 letter, 1 May \n\n1911. Nos. 2-6, pp. 31-(37)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 2 letters, 18 February and 19 April\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 3 letters, 12 February, 23 April and 26 April\n\n1912. Nos. 7-16, pp. 39-(49)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 4 letters and 1 postcard, 23 February - 26 December\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 3 letters and 2 postcards, 17 February - 24 December. The postcard dated 21 August also contains greetings from Emile Verhaeren and the postcard dated 1 April also contains greetings from Pierre Jean Jouve and Friderike Maria von Winternitz\n\n1913. Nos. 17-40, pp. 51-(72)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 11 letters and 1 postcard, 2 January - 30 October\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 10 letters and 2 postcards, 24 January - 27 August \n\n1914. Nos. 41-80, pp. 73-(156)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 18 letters and 4 postcards, 21 March - 22 December\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 15 letters and 3 postcards, 18 April - 23 December\n\n1915. Nos. 81-154, pp. 157-(300)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 26 letters and 2 postcards, 11 January - 25 December\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 35 letters and 11 postcards, 2 January - 30 December\n\n1916. Nos. 155-178, pp. 301-(340)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 10 letters, 7 January - 30 November\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 10 letters, 1 postcard and 3 telegrams, 17 January - 5 December\n\n1917. Nos. 179-196, pp. 341-(380)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 8 letters, 3 March - 29 December\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 10 letters, 18 February - 31 December\n\n1918. Nos. 197-270, pp. 381-(536)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 34 letters and 2 postcards, 1 January - 28 December\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 37 letters and 1 postcard, 4 January - 30 December. The postcard dated 11 March also contains greetings from Joseph Chapiro, Friderike Maria von Winternitz [Friderike Maria Zweig], and René Arcos\n\n1919. Nos. 271-310, pp. 537-(622)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 20 letters, 1 postcard and 2 telegrams, 2 January - 21 November\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 16 letters and 1 telegram, 2 January - 29 November\n\nAppendix:\n\nBibliographie, pp. 623-(626)\nIndex, pp. 627-(637)\nTable, p. (639)\n\n[2015]: Éditions Albin Michel, Paris\n\nRomain Rolland - Stefan Zweig. Correspondance 1920-1927. Edited with an introduction and annotations by Jean-Yves Brancy. The 10 letters by Zweig written in German were translated into French by Siegrun Barat. 730/(5)p. The book jacket contains a detail from a ca. 1920 photograph of the Palais Auersperg, Lastenstrasse, Wien (Vienna)\n\nContents:\n\nAvant-propos [Jean-Yves Brancy], p. (7)\nIntroduction [Jean-Yves Brancy], pp. 9-(28)\nSources, pp. 29-(30)\nAbréviations, pp. 31-(32)\n\nCorrespondance:\n\n1920. Nos. 1-56, pp. 33-(168)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 28 letters and 4 postcards, 4 January - 19 December\n\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 24 letters, 10 January - 30 December. The letters of 5 May [No. 21], 15 May [No. 24], and 11 December [No. 52] were translated into French by Siegrun Barat\n\n1921. Nos. 57-97, pp. 169-(253)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 17 letters and 3 postcards, 2 January - 31 December\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 18 letters and 3 postcards, 2 January - 31 December. The letters of 8 February [No. 61], 21 October [No. 90], and 6 November [91] were translated into French by Siegrun Barat. The postcard dated 1 April [No. 72] also contains greetings from Andrée Jouve, Pierre Jean Jouve, and Friderike Maria Zweig and the postcard dated 10 August [No. 84] also contains greetings from Paul Amann plus the signatures of Madeleine Rolland, Georg Fr. Nicolaï, Fernand Desprès, and Paul Castiaux\n\n1922. Nos. 98-123, pp. 255-(320)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 11 letters and 1 postcard, 21 January - 14 December\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 14 letters, 4 January - 3 December. The letters of 26 May [No. 107], 21 June [No. 109], and 3 December [No. 122] were translated into French by Siegrun Barat\n\n1923. Nos. 124-156, pp. 321-(381)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 15 letters, 1 postcard, and 1 telegram, 18 January - 3 December\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 15 letters and 1 postcard, 3 January - End of 1923 or Beginning of 1924\n\n1924. Nos. 157-191, pp. 383-(453)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 16 letters, 2 postcards, and 2 telegrams, 3 January - 19 December\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 14 letters and 1 postcard, Beginning of January - 16 December. The undated letter [No. 169] was translated into French by Siegrun Barat\n\n1925. Nos. 192-242, pp. 455-(554)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 21 letters and 1 postcard, 18 January - 17 December\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 27 letters and 2 postcards, 3 January - 30 December. The letter of 26 January [No. 194] and the postcard of 25 March [No. 206] also contain greetings from Friderike Maria Zweig\n\n1926. Nos. 243-286, pp. 555-(629)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 19 letters and 4 postcards, 8 January - 25 December. The postcard dated 26 June [No. 264] also contains greetings from Marcel Martinet and the postcard dated 1 August [No. 267] also contains greetings from Latzko. Siegrun Barat translated these greetings into French \nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 16 letters and 4 postcrads, 11 January - 30 December. The postcard dated 13 April [No. 256] also contains greetings from Friderike Maria Zweig, Pauline Masereel Paule, and Frans Masereel\n\n1927. Nos. 287-331, pp. 631-(707)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 15 letters and 4 postcards, 15 February - 25 December\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 20 letters, 4 postcards, and 2 telegrams, 27 January - 27 December. The letter of 27 January [No. 287] and the postcard dated 1 March [No. 294] also contain greetings from Friderike Maria Zweig. The telegram dated 30 March [No. 301] was translated into French by Siegrun Barat\n\nAppendix:\n\nBibliographie, pp. 709-(714)\nIndex, pp. 715-(731)\nTable, p. (733)\n\n[2016]: Éditions Albin Michel, Paris\n\nRomain Rolland - Stefan Zweig. Correspondance 1928-1940. Edited with an introduction and annotations by Jean-Yves Brancy. The letters by Zweig written in German were translated into French by Siegrun Barat. 619/(4)p. The book jacket contains a detail from a 1938 photograph of the police restraining a crowd in the Babenberger Strasse, Wien (Vienna), who were supporting Hitler, the \"new leader of Austria\", © Hulton-Deutsch Collection/Corbis, London\n\nContents:\n\nAvant-propos [Siegrun Barat and Jean-Yves Brancy], pp. 7-8\nIntroduction [Jean-Yves Brancy], pp. 9-(20)\nSources, p. (21)\nAbréviations, pp. 23-(24)\n\nCorrespondance:\n\n1928. Nos. 1-32, pp. 25-(87)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 10 letters, 4 postcards, and 1 telegram, 2 February - 18 December\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 14 letters and 3 postcards, (January?) - 5 December. The letters of 21 September [No. 25] and 3 October 9 [No. 28] were translated into French by Siegrun Barat\n\n1929. Nos.33-59, pp. 89-(135)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 8 letters and 4 postcards, 17 January - 30 December\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 10 letters and 5 postcards, 20 January - 28 December. The postcard of 6 September also contains greetings from Friderike Maria Zweig and Toshihiko Katayama\n\n1930. Nos. 60-91, pp. 137-(195)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 12 letters and 3 postcards, 20 February - 5 October\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 15 letters and 2 postcards, 3 January - 28 November\n\n1931. Nos. 92-117, pp. 197-(246)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 9 letters and 3 postcards, 5 February - 30 December\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 10 letters and 4 postcards, 8 January - 28 December\n\n1932. Nos. 118-144, pp. 247-(306)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 10 letters, 20 February - 31 December. The letter of 31 December [No. 144] was translated from German into French by Siegrun Barat\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 17 letters, 15 January - 18 December\n\n1933. Nos. 145-188, pp. 307-(386)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 13 letters, 18 January - 26 December\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 23 letters and 7 postcards, 1 January - 18 December\n\n1934. Nos. 189-212, pp. 387-(434)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 10 letters, 17 January - 26 December\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 12 letters and 2 postcards, 11 January - 21 December\n\n1935. Nos. 213-231, pp. 435-(464)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 6 letters, 29 March - 30 December\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 8 letters and 5 postcards, 29 January - 12 December\n\n1936. Nos. 232-249, pp. 465-(499)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 8 letters, 28 January - 9 December\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 9 letters and 1 postcard, 7 January - 5 December\n\n1937. Nos. 250-263, pp. 501-(531)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 5 letters, 22 February - 30 November\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 9 letters, 18 February - 7 December\n\n1938. Nos. 264-280, pp. 533-(563)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 9 letters, 15 February - 5 December\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 7 letters and 1 postcard, 16 February - 21 December\n\n1939. Nos. 281-298, pp. 565-(593)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 5 letters and 1 postcard, 17 March - 18 December\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 9 letters and 3 postcards, 10 January - 11 December\n\n1940. Nos. 299-304, pp. 595-(600)\n\nRomain Rolland to Stefan Zweig, 2 letters, 20 February and 7 April\nStefan Zweig to Romain Rolland, 3 letters and 1 postcard, 13 February - 19 April\n\nAppendix:\n\nBibliographie, pp. 601-(606)\nIndex, pp. 607-(620)\nTable, p. (621)",
