      "bibliographicCitation": "[1964]: Verlag Kurt Desch, Wien/München/Basel\n\nDeutsche Literatur im Exil. Briefe europäischer Autoren 1933-1949. Edited with a foreword and notes by Hermann Kesten. 380p. Reprinted in 1973 by the Fischer Taschenbuch Verlag, Frankfurt am Main. 315p. These are all letters written either to or by Hermann Kesten. See: Kesten, Hermann\n\nContents:\n\nVorwort, pp. 15-(23) [1973 edition, pp. 13-19]\nBriefe, pp. (25)-(372) [1973 edition, pp. 21-306]\nNamenregister, pp. 373-379 [1973 edition, pp. 307-135]. Pagination references to Friderike Maria Zweig, Lotte Zweig, and Stefan Zweig, p. 379 [1973 edition, p. 135]\n\nZweig letters or references to Stefan, Friderike Maria or Lotte Zweig\n\nStefan Zweig to Hermann Kesten, 16 June 1933, pp. 35-36 [1973 edition, pp. 27-28]\nHermann Kesten to Stefan Zweig, 21 June 1933, p. 39 [1973 edition, p. 30]\nFranz Schoenberner to Hermann Kesten, 23 June 1933, pp. 39-44. Reference to Stefan Zweig, p. 42 [1973 edition, pp. 31-34. Zweig reference, p. 33]\nFranz Schoenberner to Hermann Kesten, 3 July 1933, pp. 47-48. Reference to Stefan Zweig, p. 47 [1973 edition, pp. 36-37. Zweig reference p. 36]\nHermann Kesten to Stefan Zweig, 15 August 1933, pp. 57-58 [1973 edition, pp. 44-45]\nJoseph Roth to Hermann Kesten, 23 August 1933, p. 58. Contains a reference to Stefan Zweig [1973 edition, p. 45]\nStefan Zweig to Hermann Kesten, 13 November 1933, p. 62 [1973 edition, p. 48]\nWalter Landauer to Hermann Kesten, 8 June 1939, p. 100. Contains references to Friderike Maria Zweig [1973 edition, pp. 77-78. Friderike Maria Zweig references, pp. 77 and 78]\nStefan Zweig to Hermann Kesten, 12 June 1939, pp. 103-104 [1973 edition, pp. 80-81]\nLudwig Marcuse to Hermann Kesten, 15 June 1939, pp. 106-108. Contains a reference to Friderike Maria Zweig, p. 108 [1973 edition, pp. 82-84. Friderike Maria Zweig reference, p. 83]\nStefan Zweig to Toni Kesten, 20 September 1939, p. 111 [1973 edition, p. 86]\nHermann Kesten to Toni Kesten, 21 September 1939, pp. 112-114. No reference to Stefan Zweig [1973 edition, pp. 87-88. Reference to Stefan Zweig, p. 88]\nHermann Kesten to Toni Kesten, 12 October 1939, p. 117. Contains a reference to Stefan Zweig [1973 edition, pp. 90-91. Reference to Stefan Zweig, p. 90]\nStefan Zweig to Hermann Kesten, 31 October 1939, p. 118 [1973 edition, p. 92]\nStefan Zweig to Hermann Kesten, 24 January 1940, pp. 130-131 [1973 edition, p. 101]\nHermann Kesten to Toni Kesten, 6 June 1940, pp. 138-139. Reference to Stefan Zweig, p. 139 [1973 edition, pp. 106-107. Reference to Stefan Zweig, p. 107]\nStefan Zweig to Hermann Kesten, 20 September 1940, pp. 149-150 [1973 edition, p. 116]\nStefan Zweig to Hermann Kesten, 29 September 1940, pp. 152-153 [1973 edition, pp. 118-119]\nStefan Zweig to Hermann Kesten, 2 October 1940, pp. 154-155 [1973 edition, p. 120]\nStefan Zweig to Hermann Kesten, 31 October 1940, pp. 161-162 [1973 edition, pp. 125-126]\nStefan Zweig to Hermann Kesten, 17 November 1940, p. 167 [1973 edition, pp. 129-130]\nHermann Kesten to George Macy, 26 November 1940, pp. 168-169. Reference to Stefan Zweig, p. 168 [1973 edition, p. 131]\nStefan Zweig to Hermann Kesten, 13 December 1940, pp. 174-175 [1973 edition, pp. 135-136]\nStefan Zweig to Hermann Kesten, 9 January 1941, pp. 178-179 [1973 edition, pp. 138-139]\nStefan Zweig to Hermann Kesten, 22 February 1941, p. 181 [1973 edition, p. 140]\nStefan and Lotte Zweig to Hermann Kesten, 16 July 1941, p. 192 [1973 edition, pp. 148-149]\nStefan Zweig to Hermann Kesten, 15 August 1941, p. 196 [1973 edition, p. 152]\nStefan Zweig to Hermann Kesten, 15 January 1942, pp. 199-200 [1973 edition, p. 155]\nThomas Mann to Hermann Kesten, 4 March 1942. Contains a reference to Stefan Zweig [1973 edition, p. 157]\nThomas Mann to Hermann Kesten, 17 October 1942, pp. 221-22. Reference to Stefan Zweig, p. 222 [1973 edition, pp. 172-173. Reference to Stefan Zweig, p. 172]\nHermann Kesten to Carl Beisler, 25 July 1946, pp. 275-276. Re