      "bibliographicCitation": "\"Can a Dope Become a Denker?\" in Chess Review [New York], 12:11 [November 1944], pp. 3-4. This article was written in response to the letters of K. O. Smith and F. W. Throne to the editor of the Chess Review in the March issue.\n\nReprinted:\n\n\"Psychiatric Analysis of Chess Idiot-Savant in Stefan Zweig's Classic\" in I. A. Horowitz and P. L. Rothenberg. The Personality of Chess. New York: The Macmillan Company / London: Collier-Macmillan Limited, 1963, pp. 58-63 [Davidson's article plus the Smith and Thorne letters]. Reprinted again in: I. A. Horowitz and P. L. Rothenberg. The Complete Book of Chess. New York/London: The Macmillan Company/Collier Books, 1969, pp. 58-63",
