      "bibliographicCitation": "\"Stefan Zweig: Nowela szachowa\" in Jerzy Giżycki. Z szachami przez wieki I kraje. Warszawa: Sport I Turystyka, 1960, pp. 230-234 [2nd edition, 1972, pp. 237-241]. These pages contain excerpts from Nowela szachowa [Translated in 1956 by Jan Jeliński], a summary of the plot and 3 illustations by Daniel Mróz. The 1972 edition contains only 1 illustration\n\nTranslations:\n\nCzech: \"'Královská hra' Stefana Zweiga\" in Šachy všech dob a zemi. Translated by Vladimír Karafiát. Praha: Práce, 1975 [Edice Kotva], pp. 302-308. Contains 3 illustraions by Daniel Mróz [pp. 302, 304, 308] and 2 photographs from the 1960 film \"Schachnovelle\" starring Curd Jürgens and Mario Adorf\n\nEnglish: \"Stefan Zweig's 'The Royal Game'\" in A History of Chess. Translated by A. Wojciechowski et al. London: Abbey Library, 1972 [Revised edition 1977], pp. 257-262. Contains 3 illustrations by Daniel Mróz\n\nGerman: \"Stefan Zweigs 'Schachnovelle'\" in Schach zu allen Zeiten. Translated by Maria Wolczacka and Malgorzata Bester. Zürich/Frankfurt am main et al.: Stauffacher Verlag, 1967, pp. 271-277",
