      "name": {
        "@value": "ʿĪd, Ḥasan",
        "@language": "ar"
      },
      "sourceTextId": 33099,
      "datePublished": "2010",
      "allYears": [
        1970,
        2010
      ],
      "timePeriod": "contemporary",
      "publisher": {
        "@id": "klawiter:publisher/house%20D%C4%81r%20al-Hil%C4%81l",
        "@type": "schema:Organization",
        "name": "house Dār al-Hilāl"
      },
      "locationCreated": {
        "@id": "klawiter:place/Menlo%20Park%2C%20CA",
        "@type": "schema:Place",
        "name": "Menlo Park, CA"
      },
      "inLanguage": "ar",
      "languageName": "Arabic",
      "numberOfPages": 178,
      "categories": [
        "Secondary Literature / Authors (Arabic)"
      ],
      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "ʿĪd, Ḥasan, \"Asʾilah khaṭīrah ḥawla \"Junūn al-ḥubb\": Hal shawwahat al-Hilāl Stīfān Zfāyj?\" [Grave Questions about \"Love's Madness\": Has al-Hilāl Distorted Stefan Zweig?], in: facebook [Menlo Park, CA], 17 October 2010\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttps://ar-ar.facebook.com/permalink.php?story_fbid=122091801183080&id=102275113146314\n\nhttps://ar-ar.facebook.com/notes/akhbar-eladab/%D8%A3%D8%B3%D8%A6%D9%84%D8%A9-%D8%AE%D8%B7%D9%8A%D8%B1%D8%A9-%D8%AD%D9%88%D9%84-%D8%AC%D9%86%D9%88%D9%86-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AD%D8%A8-%D9%87%D9%84-%D8%B4%D9%88%D9%87%D8%AA-%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%87%D9%84%D8%A7%D9%84-%D8%B3%D8%AA%D9%8A%D9%81%D8%A7%D9%86-%D8%B2%D9%81%D9%80%D8%A7%D9%8A%D8%AC-/480998898063/?fref=mentions\n\nThis is a review of two Arabic titles published by the Cairene publishing house Dār al-Hilāl, Junūn al-ḥubb [Love's Madness] and Qulūb taḥtariq: maʾsāt insāniyyah muʾaththirah [Hearts Burning. A Moving Human Tragedy]. The first volume, Junūn al-ḥubb, comprises two of Stefan Zweig's novellas, i.e. \"24 [Arbaʿ wa-ʿishrūn] sāʿah fī ḥayāt imraʾah\" [Vierundzwanzig Stunden aus dem Leben einer Frau] and \"Junūn al-ḥubb\" [Brennendes Geheimnis], while the second volume, Qulūb taḥtariq, is one of the two or more existing Arabic translations of Ungeduld des Herzens.\n\nJunūn al-ḥubb [Vierundzwanzig Stunden aus dem Leben einer Frau & Brennendes Geheimnis]. Edited by Maḥmūd Qāsim. 214p\n\nQulūb taḥtariq: maʾsāt insāniyyah muʾaththirah [Ungeduld des Herzens]. Translated with a biographical foreword by Dār al-Hilāl. 178p. Illustrated. 1970",
      "sourceBlobId": 3
    },
