      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "\"'Imraʾat' Stīfān Zfāygh fī khaybat al-sāʿāt al-24 (al-arbaʿ waʾl-ʿishrīn) masraḥiyyan\" [Stefan Zweig’s “Woman” in the Disillusionment of the 24 Hours as Seen on Stage] in Al-Ḥayāt [The Life] [International print edition] [London], No.? [26 August 2015], p.?\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://alturl.com/6vepw\n\nThis is a review of Christine Khandjian’s and Stéphane Ly-Cuong’s musical adaptation of Stefan Zweig’s \"Vingt-quatre heures de la vie d'une femme\" [Vierundzwanzig Stunden aus dem Leben einer Frau], directed by Franck Berthier, starring, among others, by Isabelle Georges, Frederik Steenbrink and Olivier Ruidavet, and staged at the Théâtre La Bruyère in Paris from the 1st of July to the 1st of August 2015\n\nThe poster for the play is online:\n\nhttp://www.theatrelabruyere.com/spectacles/24heures.php",
      "sourceBlobId": 3
    },
