      "mainCategory": "Historical Studies",
      "bibliographicCitation": "[1943]: Cassell and Company Limited, London\n\nThe World of Yesterday. An Autobiography [Die Welt von Gestern. Erinnerungen eines Europäers]. Translated by Benjamin W. Huebsch and Helmut Ripperger. 339p. Illustrated. Bibliography of Stefan\nZweig’s works, pp. 331-332\n\nSubsequent editions:\n\n1943: The Viking Press, New York. xiv/455p. Illustrated. Zweig bibliography, pp. 443-445\n\n1944: Cassell and Company Limited, London., 339p. \n\n1944: Cassell and Company Limited, London/Toronto/ Melbourne/Sydney. 310p. 2 printings inn Sydney, Australia\n\n1947: Cassell and Company Limited, London. xiv/445p. \n\n1953: Cassell and Company Limited, London. xi/449p. [Hallam Edition]. See: The Complete Works of Stefan Zweig. Vol. 10\n\n1964: University of Nebraska Press, Lincoln, NE. Introduction by Harry Zohn. xxiii/445p. Cover design by Jack Brodle. Cover drawing of St. Stefan's Dome by Erwin Puchinger. Paperback edition [A Bison Book, BB 181]. Harry Zohn's introduction, pp. v-xii. / 1966: 13th impression. Cover design by Jungsun Whang. Cover drawing \"Der Zwang\", woodcut by Frans Masereel\n\n1977: The Arden Press, New York. xiv/445p. [Reprinted of the 3rd edition of 1943 \n\n1987: Cassell and Company Limited, London. 339p. [Cassell Biographies]. The impressum incorrectly lists the translators as \"Cedar and Eden Paul\"",
