      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "\"Fāris Yūwākīm: Inhiyār al-ʿarab badaʾa fī ʾl-sabʿīnāt maʿa mā summiya «ʿaṣr al-infitāḥ»: baʿda ṣudūr tarjamatihī li-kitāb «ʿUnf al-diktātūriyyah» li-Stīfān Zfāygh\" [Fares Youakim: \"The Decline of the Arabs Started in the Seventies with What Then Was Called the 'Age of Opening Up', Taking Up the Publication of 'The Violence of Dictatorship', His Translation of Stefan Zweig's Book 'The Right to Heresy: Castellio against Calvin'\"], in Al-Sharq al-Awsaṭ [The Middle East] [London] No. 12626 [23 June 2013], p. ?. Published by the Al-Majmūʿah al-Suʿūdiyyah li-l-Abḥāth waʾl-Taswīq [Saudi Research and Marketing Group (SRMG)], [Landan] London. Sawsan al-Abṭaḥ [Sawsan al Abtah] is the journalist who wrote the article and interviewed Fāris Yūwākīm [Fares Youakim]. Since most of the article consists of direct quotes from the interviewed Fares Youakim, it seems appropriate to mention Youakim as the second author/second originator of the text\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://alturl.com/m39ok",
      "sourceBlobId": 3
