      "sourcePageId": 4511,
      "pageNamespace": 0,
      "name": {
        "@value": "Farīd, Māhir Shafīq",
        "@language": "ar"
      },
      "sourceTextId": 32879,
      "datePublished": "2014",
      "allYears": [
        1905,
        1917,
        1962,
        1992,
        2002,
        2014
      ],
      "timePeriod": "contemporary",
      "publisher": {
        "@id": "klawiter:publisher/the%20%20Al-Majm%C5%AB%CA%BFah%20al-Su%CA%BF%C5%ABdiyyah%20li-l-Ab%E1%B8%A5%C4%81th%20wa%CA%BEl-Tasw%C4%ABq",
        "@type": "schema:Organization",
        "name": "the  Al-Majmūʿah al-Suʿūdiyyah li-l-Abḥāth waʾl-Taswīq"
      },
      "locationCreated": {
        "@id": "klawiter:place/London",
        "@type": "schema:Place",
        "name": "London",
        "sameAs": "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q84"
      },
      "allLocations": [
        "London",
        "New York",
        "Cairo"
      ],
      "inLanguage": "ar",
      "languageName": "Arabic",
      "categories": [
        "Secondary Literature / Authors (Arabic)"
      ],
      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "\"Stīfān Zfāyj.. yaʿūd ilā dāʾirat al-ḍawʾ : al-manfā athnāʾa fatrat al-nāziyyah ḥawwalahū ilā mughtarib abadī wa-rajul bi-lā waṭan\" [Stefan Zweig Returns into the Spotlight: the Exile during the Nazi Period Turned Him into an Eternal Alien and a Man without Homeland] in Al-Sharq al-Awsaṭ [The Middle East] [London] No. 13118, 28 October 2014, p. ?. Published by the Al-Majmūʿah al-Suʿūdiyyah li-l-Abḥāth waʾl-Taswīq [Saudi Research and Marketing Group (SRMG)], [Landan] London\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://archive.aawsat.com/details.asp?section=19&article=792378&issueno=13118#.WcU2RbiW62B\n\nThis is a review of George Prochnik’s biography The Impossible Exile. Stefan Zweig at the End of the World [New York: Other Press, 2014]. The reviewer Māhir Shafīq Farīd quotes as outstanding witnesses of the influence Stefan Zweig's works had on Arab intellectuals two Egyptian thinkers: [1]. the philosopher 'Abdurrahmān Badawi [ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Badawī] (1917-2002), who testified to Zweig's greatness in the chapter \"ʿAbqarī yantaḥir\" [A Genius Committing Suicide] of his book Al-Mawt waʾl-ʿabqariyyah [Death and Genius]. Cairo: Maktabat al-Nahḍah al-Miṣriyyah, 2nd edition, 1962, pp. 80-96. See:\n\nand [2]. the writer Yaḥyā Ḥaqqī (1905-1992), who praised Zweig in the preface \"Muqaddimah\" to his translation Qiṣṣatān min al-adab al-almānī [Two Stories from German Literature]: Stefan Zweig's \"Schachnovelle\" [Lāʿib al-shaṭranj] and Thomas Mann's \"Tonio Krüger\" [Ṭūniyū Krūjir]. See: http://zweig.fredonia.edu/index.php?title=%E1%B8%A4aqq%C4%AB%2C_Ya%E1%B8%A5y%C4%81>",
      "sourceBlobId": 3
    },
    {
      "@type": [
        "schema:ScholarlyArticle",
        "klawiter:SecondaryLiteratureEntry"
      ],
      "@id": "klawiter:entry/4512",
      "entryType": "secondary-literature",
      "sourcePageId": 4512,
      "pageNamespace": 0,
      "name": {
        "@value": "\"Stīfān Zfāyj: 1881 tuwuffiya sanat 1942 al-Nimsā\" [Stefan Zweig, 1881, died 1942, Austria] in Abjad [Abjjad / Alphabet] [Amman], retrieved on 23 September 2017",
        "@language": "ar"
      },
      "sourceTextId": 34358,
      "datePublished": "1881",
      "allYears": [
        1881,
        1942,
        2017
      ],
      "timePeriod": "lifetime",
      "publisher": {
        "@id": "klawiter:publisher/community%20contribute%20short%20reviews%20and%20critiques%20of%20the%20books",
        "@type": "schema:Organization",
        "name": "community contribute short reviews and critiques of the books"
      },
      "locationCreated": {
        "@id": "klawiter:place/Stefan%20Zweig",
        "@type": "schema:Place",
        "name": "Stefan Zweig"
      },
      "inLanguage": "ar",
      "languageName": "Arabic",
      "categories": [
        "Secondary Literature / Titles (Arabic)"
      ],
      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "\"Stīfān Zfāyj: 1881 tuwuffiya sanat 1942 al-Nimsā\" [Stefan Zweig, 1881, died 1942, Austria] in Abjad [Abjjad / Alphabet] [Amman], retrieved on 23 September 2017\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttps://www.abjjad.com/author/2519007232/%D8%B3%D8%AA%D9%8A%D9%81%D8%A7%D9%86-%D8%B2%D9%81%D8%A7%D9%8A%D8%AC/books\n\nAbjad [Abjjad / Alphabet] is an Arab online community, the company head quarters of which are based in Amman, Jordan. The members of the online community contribute short reviews and critiques of the books they read. One entry is dedicated to Stefan Zweig and his oeuvre under the afore-mentioned heading \"Stīfān Zfāyj: 1881 tuwuffiya sanat 1942 al-Nimsā\" [Stefan Zweig, 1881, died 1942, Austria]. Altogether [as of 8 December 2017] there are fourteen translations of Zweig's works into Arabic which are presented to the general reader",
      "sourceBlobId": 3
    },
