      ],
      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "[1]. \"Dhālika al-inhiyār fī ʿĀlam al-ams li-Stīfān Zfāyj\" [Such a Breakdown in Stefan Zweig's The World of Yesterday] in Al-Ḥiwār al-mutamaddin [The Civilized Dialogue] [Iraq], No. 2613 [11 April 2009]. \"Al-Ḥiwār al-mutamaddin\" [The Civilized Dialogue] is an Iraqi website\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://www.ahewar.org/debat/show.art.asp?aid=168573\n\nAl-Ḥiwār al-mutamaddin [The Civilized Dialogue] is an Iraqi website\n\nLater republished twice without indication of the original source:\n\n[2]. \"Dhālika al-inhiyār fī ʿĀlam al-ams li-Stīfān Zfāyj\" [Such a Breakdown in Stefan Zweig's The World of Yesterday] in Manārāt [Manarat / Lighthouses] [Baghdad], Vol. 9: No. 2477 [9 May 2012], Stefan Zweig, pp. 6-7. Manārāt [Manarat / Lighthouses] is a weekly cultural supplement to the Iraqi daily Al-Madā [The Reach]\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://www.almadasupplements.com/pdf/05-2477/21.pdf\n\nhttp://www.almadasupplements.net/news.php?action=view&id=4605&spell=0&highlight=%D0%E1%DF+%C7%E1%C7%E4%E5%ED%C7%D1#sthash.Y0mi5Tvh.dpbs\n\nThis is a review of the Arabic translation\n\nʿĀlam al-ams [Die Welt von Gestern. Erinnerungen eines Europäers]. Translated into Arabic by ʿĀrif Ḥudhayfah [Arif Hudaifa]. 343p. Damascus/Beirut/Baghdad: Dār al-Madā li-l-Thaqāfah waʾl-Nashr [Al Mada Publishing Company F.K.A.], 2007\n\n[3]. \"Dhālika al-inhiyār fī ʿĀlam al-ams li-Stīfān Zfāyj\" [Such a Breakdown in Stefan Zweig's The World of Yesterday] in Ḥizb al-irādah al-shaʿbiyyah / People's Will Party [Damascus], 22 July 2014\n\nḤizb al-irādah al-shaʿbiyyah [People's Will Party] is the website of the Syrian political party of the same name, a breakaway of the Syrian communists\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://kassioun.org/art-and-culture/item/8968-2014-07-22-20-03-29\n\nThis is a review of the Arabic translation\n\nʿĀlam al-ams [Die Welt von Gestern. Erinnerungen eines Europäers]. Translated into Arabic by ʿĀrif Ḥudhayfah [Arif Hudaifa]. 343 p. Damascus/Beirut/Baghdad: Dār al-Madā li-l-Thaqāfah waʾl-Nashr [Al Mada Publishing Company F.K.A.], 2007",
      "sourceBlobId": 4
    },
    {
      "@type": [
        "schema:ScholarlyArticle",
        "klawiter:SecondaryLiteratureEntry"
      ],
      "@id": "klawiter:entry/4603",
      "entryType": "secondary-literature",
      "sourcePageId": 4603,
      "pageNamespace": 0,
      "name": {
        "@value": "Al-Fallāḥī, Fāṭimah / Elfalahy, Fatima",
        "@language": "ar"
      },
      "sourceTextId": 33104,
      "datePublished": "2011",
      "allYears": [
        2011,
        2012
      ],
      "timePeriod": "contemporary",
      "inLanguage": "ar",
      "languageName": "Arabic",
      "numberOfPages": 4,
      "categories": [
        "Secondary Literature / Authors (Arabic)"
      ],
      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "\"Al-ʿĀlam alladhī aḥbabnāhu wallā ilā ghayr rajʿah. Wa-mā yaʾtī minhū [recte: baʿdahū] laysa bi-wusʿinā an nataḥammalahū. Wa-mā jadwā an yuwāṣila al-marʾ ḥayātan shāḥiba. - Stīfān Tsfāygh - Stīfān Zfāngh [sic] - min al-adab al-ʿālamī (al-maktabah al-iliktrūniyyah) [The World We Loved Has Gone beyond Recall. What Will Come of It [recte: after It] We Are Not Able to Endure. What Is the Benefit of Continuing a Dull Life? - Stefan Zweig (from World Literature / The Electronic Library)] in Al-Ḥiwār al-mutamaddin [The Civilized Dialogue] [Iraq], 21 November 2011. \"Al-Ḥiwār al-mutamaddin\" [The Civilized Dialogue] is an Iraqi website\n\nPublished online:\nhttp://www.m.ahewar.org/s.asp?aid=284319&r=0\n\nLater re-edited and split into five separate texts: an article under Fāṭimah al-Fallāḥī's own name [1] plus four shorter anonymously published texts [2-5]. All five texts appeared in a special issue of Manārāt [Lighthouses], dedicated to Stefan Zweig. Manārāt is a weekly cultural supplement to the Iraqi daily Al-Madā [The Reach]\n\n[1]. \"Stīfān Zfāyj waʾl-ʿālam alladhī aḥbabnāhu\" [Stefan Zweig and the World We Loved] in Manārāt [Manarat / Lighthouses] [Baghdad], Vol. 9: No. 2477 [9 May 2012], Stefan Zweig, pp. 2-3\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://www.almadasupplements.com/pdf/05-2477/21.pdf\n\nhttp://www.almadasupplements.net/news.php?action=view&id=4607#sthash.BFScAVvi.oTpcuv8w.dpbs\n\n[2]. \"Raʾy Stīfān Zfāyj biʾl-ākhar\" [Stefan Zweig's Opinion of Others] in Manārāt [Manarat / Lighthouses] [Baghdad], Vol. 9: No. 2477 [9 May 2012], Stefan Zweig, p. 4\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://www.almadasupplements.com/pdf/05-2477/21.pdf\n\n[3]. \"Ahamm aʿmāl Stīfān Zfāyj\" [The Most Important Works of Stefan Zweig] in Manārāt [Manarat / Lighthouses] [Baghdad], Vol. 9: No. 2477 [9 May 2012], Stefan Zweig, pp. 10-12\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://www.almadasupplements.com/pdf/05-2477/21.pdf\n\nhttp://www.almadasupplements.com/news.php?action=view&id=4601#sthash.B6fYpMCd.dpbs\n\n[4]. \"Raʾy al-ākharīn fī aʿmālihī\" [The Others' Opinion of His Works] in Manārāt [Manarat / Lighthouses] [Baghdad], Vol. 9: No. 2477 [9 May 2012], Stefan Zweig, p. 12\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://www.almadasupplements.com/pdf/05-2477/21.pdf\n\nhttp://almadasupplements.com/news.php?action=view&id=4600#sthash.6NxUiCpJ.bt0FvJYZ.dpbs\n\n[5]. \"Intiḥār Stīfān Zfāyj\" [Stefan Zweig's Suicide] in Manārāt [Manarat / Lighthouses] [Baghdad], Vol. 9: No. 2477 [9 May 2012], Stefan Zweig, p. 12\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://www.almadasupplements.com/pdf/05-2477/21.pdf\n\nhttp://almadasupplements.com/news.php?action=view&id=4599#sthash.QQEyjjnF.dpbs",
      "sourceBlobId": 3
    },
