    {
      "@type": [
        "schema:Book",
        "klawiter:FictionEntry"
      ],
      "@id": "klawiter:entry/4608",
      "entryType": "fiction",
      "sourcePageId": 4608,
      "pageNamespace": 0,
      "name": {
        "@value": "The Royal Game and Other Stories / Indonesian",
        "@language": "id"
      },
      "sourceTextId": 34028,
      "author": {
        "@id": "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q78491",
        "@type": "schema:Person",
        "name": "Stefan Zweig"
      },
      "datePublished": "2017",
      "timePeriod": "contemporary",
      "publisher": {
        "@id": "klawiter:publisher/title%20of%20the%20book%20seems%20to%20indicate%20a%20mere%20Indonesian%20reedition",
        "@type": "schema:Organization",
        "name": "title of the book seems to indicate a mere Indonesian reedition"
      },
      "locationCreated": {
        "@id": "klawiter:place/Yogyakarta",
        "@type": "schema:Place",
        "name": "Yogyakarta"
      },
      "inLanguage": "id",
      "languageName": "Indonesian",
      "numberOfPages": 226,
      "translator": {
        "@id": "klawiter:person/Maria%20Vregina%20and%20Aprilia%20Rizqi%20Parwidanti",
        "@type": "schema:Person",
        "name": "Maria Vregina and Aprilia Rizqi Parwidanti"
      },
      "categories": [
        "Fiction / Volumes (Indonesian)"
      ],
      "mainCategory": "Fiction",
      "bibliographicCitation": "[2017]: Papyrus Publishing, Yogyakarta\n\nThe Royal Game and Other Stories [Schachnovelle und andere Erzählungen]. Translated into Indonesian by Maria Vregina and Aprilia Rizqi Parwidanti. Edited by Wayan Darmaputra. (8)/226p.\n\nAt first glance, the English title of the book seems to indicate a mere Indonesian reedition of one of the English translations. Yet, the ads of the Indonesian booksellers classify the text as a translation (\"terjemahan\") , reporting even the names of the two Indonesian translators (\"penerjemah\"), Maria Vregina and Aprilia Rizqi Parwidanti . Moreover, they state expressly that the language (\"bahasa\") of the text is \"Indonesia\" , which stands for \"bahasa Indonesia\", the official designation of the Indonesian language. Cf. as well:\n\nhttps://www.google.de/search?q=%22The+Royal+Game+and+Other+Stories%22+Papyrus+Publishing&tbm=isch&source=iu&pf=m&ictx=1&fir=B2wRd1MDKw9vFM%253A%252CjeQ2TA33p-IQvM%252C_&usg=__XT7lvYdOPNkO-FvARLa-EU9e-FA%3D&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwi31oqLmunWAhWRZlAKHREyABkQ9QEIPjAD&biw=1400&bih=921#imgrc=B2wRd1MDKw9vFM:\n\n-------------------------------------------",
      "sourceBlobId": 3
    },
