      "pageNamespace": 0,
      "name": {
        "@value": "Al-Maʿmarī, Sulaymān ibn ʿAlī / Ḥamad, Hudā // Almamari, Sulaiman / Hamad, Huda",
        "@language": "ar"
      },
      "sourceTextId": 34593,
      "datePublished": "2017",
      "timePeriod": "contemporary",
      "inLanguage": "ar",
      "languageName": "Arabic",
      "numberOfPages": 78,
      "categories": [
        "Secondary Literature / Authors (Arabic)"
      ],
      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "\"Riwāyat 'Lāʿib al-shaṭranj' li-l-adīb al-nimsāwī Stīfān Sfāygh\" [The Novel \"The Royal Game\" by the Austrian Man of Letters Stefan Zweig]. Presented by Sulaymān ibn ʿAlī al-Maʿmarī [Sulaiman Almamari]. With the guest, the writer Hudā Ḥamad [Huda Hamad], in Barnāmij kitāb aʿjabanī [Program 'A Book Which I Liked'] [Muscat] session 812 [6 June 2017], 17 min. 33 sec. The daily program \"Barnāmij kitāb aʿjabanī\" [Program 'A Book Which I Liked'] is broadcasted at 9:20 AM and 6:15PM (local time) by \"Radio Sultanate Oman\" [Idhāʿat Salṭanat ʿUmān] from Muscat [Masqaṭ]. In about a quarter of an hour, a book is presented to the listeners during an interview with a reader thereof invited to the session\n\nPublished online (audio streaming):\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0-_weYUQLWk\n\nThis is a review of the Arabic translation of Stefan Zweig's \"Schachnovelle\":\n\nLāʿib al-shaṭranj [Schachnovelle]. Translated by Saḥar Sattālah. 78p. Tunis: Maskīliyānā li-l-Nashr waʾl-Tawzīʿ [Masciliana Editions], 2017",
      "sourceBlobId": 3
    },
