      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "[1]. \"Al-Thaqāfah al-almāniyyah fī ʾl-ḥiqbah al-nāziyyah wa-burūz ẓāhirat al-manfā\" [German Culture in the Nazi Period and the Emergence of the Phenomenon of Exile] in Kīkā li-l-adab al-ʿālamī [kikah.com. For Free Culture & Tolerance [s.l.], 1 May 2012. The essay describes the atrocities of Nazism that forced the intellectual elite, among them Stefan Zweig, out of Germany and the German-speaking countries into exile\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://alturl.com/hid6b\n\n'[2]. \"Kālfin: al-iṣlāḥī alladhī taḥawwala dīktātūran\" [Calvin, the Reformer Who Turned into a Dictator] in Al-Markaz al-Lubnānī li-l-Abḥāth waʾl-Istishārāt [Lebanese Center for Research and Consulting] [Sidon], 17 April 2013\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://www.center-lcrc.org/index.php?s=17&id=7736\n\nThis is a review of the Arabic translation:\n\nʿUnf al-diktātūriyyah [The Violence of Dictatorship = Castellio gegen Calvin oder Ein Gewissen gegen die Gewalt]. Translated by Fāris Yūwākīm [Fares Youakim]. 223p. 1st edition. Beirut: Dār al-Furāt li-l-Nashr waʾl-Tawzīʿ, 2013",
