      ],
      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "\"Stīfān Tsfāygh yatadhakkar «ʿĀlam al-ams» wa-sāʿāt al-hubūṭ waʾl-ṣuʿūd\" [Stefan Zweig Remembers \"The World of Yesterday\" and the Hours of Decline and Ascent] in Ṣaḥafī [Journalist] [Amman], 27 November 2007\n\nṢaḥafī [Journalist] is a Jordanian website published by the Markaz Awān li-l-Istishārāt al-Iʿlāmiyyah al-ʿArabiyyah [Amman]\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://alturl.com/rhjdv\n\nThis review, the author of which is not indicated, was subsequently published anonymously in the Jordanian website \"Ṣaḥafī\" [Journalist] [Amman]. It was orginally written by Bandar ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd and published in the Damascene periodical \"Al-Ḥayāt\". This is a review of the Arabic translation:\n\nʿĀlam al-ams [Die Welt von Gestern. Erinnerungen eines Europäers]. Translated into Arabic by ʿĀrif Ḥudhayfah [Arif Hudaifa]. 343p. Damascus/Beirut/Baghdad: Dār al-Madā li-l-Thaqāfah waʾl-Nashr [Al Mada Publishing Company F.K.A.], 2007",
      "sourceBlobId": 3
    },
