      "bibliographicCitation": "[1992]: Karelian Opera Theater, Petrozavodsk\n\nAmok [An opera based on Stefan Zweig's novella \"Der Amokläufer\"]\n\nLanguage: Russian\nLibretto by: Viktor Guin and Boris Sinkin\nMusic by: Boris Sinkin\nCast: Viktor Piščaev [of the Mikhailovsky Ballet and Opera Theatre, St. Petersburg], Elena Mirtova [of the Kirov (Mariinsky) Opera and Ballet Theatre, St. Petersburg], Anatoli Buganov [of the Kirov (Mariinsky) Opera and Ballet Theatre, St. Petersburg] et al.\nProduction sponsored by the Nevskaia Perspektiva Association of St. Petersburg, Russia\nFirst performance on 11 February 1992. Performed in the St. Petersburg Opera Theatre in 1993\nAvailable on tape and videotape \n\n[1995]: La Compagnie du Loup, Noisiel / Théâtre du Bourg Neuf, Avignon\n\nAmok [A stage production based on Stefan Zweig's novella \"Der Amokläufer\"]. See: Nocturnes\n\nLanguage: French\nDirector: Jean-Marc Galéra\nStaging producer: Régis Gayrard\nCast: Jean-Marc Galéra, Victor Mazzilli, Raïna Paris et al.\nMusic by: David Venitucci\nLighting by: Pierre Negre\nCostumes by: Marie-Paule Louis\nPremiere in Avignon: 9 July-3 August 1995\nFurther performances: [1]. Théâtre de la Source, Bègles, 21 February-2 March 1996. [2]. Théâtre du Rio (Compagnie Yvon Chaix), Grenoble, 2-13 April 1996. [3]. L'Espace Senghor, Bruxelles, 26 November-7 December 1996\nSee: Bulletin de l'Association Stefan Zweig [Nanterre], No. 6 [November/December 1995], pp. 12-13; No. 7 [January/February 1996], pp. 12-16; No. 9 [May/June 1996], p. 9; No. 10 [July/August 1996], p. 8",
