      ],
      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "\"Il progjet Grande Vuere. In publicazion il librut plurilengâl sul 1914\" [The Great War Project. Forthcoming: the Multilingual Book about 1914] in Voce isontina : settimanale dell'arcidiocesi di Gorizia [The Voice of the Isonzo: Weekly of the Archdiocese of Gorizia] [Gorizia], Vol. 51, No. 11 [21 March 2015], p. 13\n\nAlthough the announced research project \"Grande Vuere\" [Great War] deals with World War I and its consequences for the Italian province of Friuli Venezia Giulia and, therefore, it might in a strict sense not be counted under secondary literature about Stefan Zweig and his oeuvre, nevertheless, the motto of the project is a quotation taken from the Die Welt von Gestern. Erinnerungen eines Europäers and rendered into the Friulian language, thereby documenting the moral weight and cultural impact Stefan Zweig's autobiography wields in the assessment of World War I on a global level in a multitude of language communities, in this case the Friulian-speaking region Friuli Venezia Giulia of north-eastern Italy\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://www.arlef.it/download/stampe-par-furlan/voce_isontina_21_03_2015_.pdf\n\nhttp://www.voceisontina.eu/content/download/87464%2F1984965%2Ffile/15-11-2103.pdf",
      "sourceBlobId": 3
    },
    {
      "@type": [
        "schema:ScholarlyArticle",
        "klawiter:SecondaryLiteratureEntry"
      ],
      "@id": "klawiter:entry/4864",
      "entryType": "secondary-literature",
      "sourcePageId": 4864,
      "pageNamespace": 0,
      "name": {
        "@value": "\"Dāʿish al-swīsriyyah\" [The Swiss Daesh] in Ṣawt al-yasār al-ʿirāqī [The Voice of the Iraqi Left] [Schwäbisch Gmünd, Germany?], 4 February 2015",
        "@language": "ar"
      },
      "sourceTextId": 35256,
      "datePublished": "2015",
      "allYears": [
        2013,
        2015
      ],
      "timePeriod": "contemporary",
      "publisher": {
        "@id": "klawiter:publisher/223p.%201st%20edition",
        "@type": "schema:Organization",
        "name": "223p. 1st edition"
      },
      "locationCreated": {
        "@id": "klawiter:place/Beirut",
        "@type": "schema:Place",
        "name": "Beirut",
        "sameAs": "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3820"
      },
      "inLanguage": "ar",
      "languageName": "Arabic",
      "numberOfPages": 223,
      "categories": [
        "Secondary Literature / Authors (Arabic)"
      ],
      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "\"Dāʿish al-swīsriyyah\" [The Swiss Daesh] in Ṣawt al-yasār al-ʿirāqī [The Voice of the Iraqi Left] [Schwäbisch Gmünd, Germany?], 4 February 2015\n\nThe reviewer compares the religious rigor of Calvin's Geneva with the fanaticism of the so-called \"Islamic State\" in present-day Syria and Iraq\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://saotaliassar.org/01012015/HamzaAlHassan0127.htm\n\nThis is a review of the Arabic translation:\n\nʿUnf al-diktātūriyyah [The Violence of Dictatorship = Castellio gegen Calvin oder Ein Gewissen gegen die Gewalt]. Translated by Fāris Yūwākīm [Fares Youakim]. 223p. 1st edition. Beirut: Dār al-Furāt li-l-Nashr waʾl-Tawzīʿ, 2013",
      "sourceBlobId": 3
    },
    {
      "@type": [
        "schema:ScholarlyArticle",
        "klawiter:SecondaryLiteratureEntry"
      ],
      "@id": "klawiter:entry/4865",
      "entryType": "secondary-literature",
      "sourcePageId": 4865,
      "pageNamespace": 0,
      "name": {
        "@value": "Zakī, ʿAbd al-Zahrah",
        "@language": "ar"
      },
      "sourceTextId": 34573,
      "datePublished": "2015",
      "allYears": [
        2013,
        2015
      ],
      "timePeriod": "contemporary",
      "publisher": {
        "@id": "klawiter:publisher/Wid%C4%81d%20Far%E1%B8%A5%C4%81n",
        "@type": "schema:Organization",
        "name": "Widād Farḥān"
      },
      "locationCreated": {
        "@id": "klawiter:place/Beirut",
        "@type": "schema:Place",
        "name": "Beirut",
        "sameAs": "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3820"
      },
      "inLanguage": "ar",
      "languageName": "Arabic",
      "numberOfPages": 223,
      "categories": [
        "Secondary Literature / Authors (Arabic)"
      ],
      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "\"Kamā law anna bika jūʿan li-ltihām al-bashar\" [As If There Were a Hunger in You to Devour Human Beings!] in Bānūrāmā : nāfidhatuka ʿalā ʾl-ʿālam [Panorama Newspaper. Your Window to the World] [Baghdad / Parramatta, NSW, Australia], Vol. 8, No. ? [2 December 2015], pp. ??\n\nThe Iraqi daily Bānūrāmā [Panorama] is published by Widād Farḥān\n\nStarting with a long quote from Castellio, the reviewer compares the \"medieval\" religious intolerance of Calvin's Geneva and the Inquisition with the same kind of fanaticism practised by Al-Qaeda and their ilk in present-day Muslim countries. Muslims, and especially the Arabs among them, should follow the example of the Christians and \"liberate their religion from this criminal way of denouncing others as heretics\"\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttps://panoramanews.net/index.php/ar/module-positions/abdulzahra-zaki/949-2015-12-02-12-29-04\n\nThis is a review of the Arabic translation:\n\nʿUnf al-diktātūriyyah [The Violence of Dictatorship = Castellio gegen Calvin oder Ein Gewissen gegen die Gewalt]. Translated by Fāris Yūwākīm [Fares Youakim]. 223p. 1st edition. Beirut: Dār al-Furāt li-l-Nashr waʾl-Tawzīʿ, 2013",
      "sourceBlobId": 3
    },
    {
      "@type": [
        "schema:ScholarlyArticle",
        "klawiter:SecondaryLiteratureEntry"
      ],
      "@id": "klawiter:entry/4866",
      "entryType": "secondary-literature",
      "sourcePageId": 4866,
      "pageNamespace": 0,
      "name": {
        "@value": "Walad al-Ṣiddīq, Mīlūd / Ould Seddik, Miloud",
        "@language": "ar"
      },
      "sourceTextId": 34577,
      "datePublished": "2015",
      "allYears": [
        2015,
        2017
      ],
      "timePeriod": "contemporary",
      "locationCreated": {
        "@id": "klawiter:place/Cairo",
        "@type": "schema:Place",
        "name": "Cairo",
        "sameAs": "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q85"
      },
      "inLanguage": "ar",
      "languageName": "Arabic",
      "categories": [
        "Secondary Literature / Authors (Arabic)"
      ],
      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "\"Al-Diktārūriyyah : aw al-intiqāl naḥwa ʾl-majhūl : dirāsah waṣfiyyah taḥlīliyyah li-khaṣāʾiṣ al-diktātūriyyāt wa-kayfiyyat muwājahatihā\" [Dictatorship or: The Transition towards the Unknown. Descriptive-Analytical Study of the Characteristics of Dictatorships and the Way to Confront Them] in African Journal of Political Science (AJPS) / Revue africaine de science politique / Al-Majallah al-afrīqiyyah li-l-ʿulūm al-siyāsiyyah [Pretoria / Cairo?], Vol. 20?, No. 1? [28 July 2015], pp. ??.\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://www.maspolitiques.com/ar/index.php/ar/flexicontact/2017-02-06-17-54-23/741-dirasssss\n\nIn a general critique of dictatorship, the Algerian political scientist Mīlūd Walad al-Ṣiddīq [Miloud Ould Seddik] calls Stefan Zweig's Castellio gegen Calvin oder Ein Gewissen gegen die Gewalt one of the most impressive artistic treatments of the subject, relying thereby on the judgment the British-Iraqi journalist Fāḍil al-Sulṭānī [Fadhil Assultani] gave in his review of the Arabic translation thereof \n\nSee:",
      "sourceBlobId": 3
    },
