      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "[1]. \"Al-Diktātūriyyah al-muzdahirah fī ʾl-'Irāq\" [The Flourishing Dictatorship in Iraq] in Al-Ḥiwār al-mutamaddin [The Civilized Dialogue] [Iraq], 24 March 2015\n\nAl-Ḥiwār al-mutamaddin [The Civilized Dialogue] is an Iraqi website\n\nTaking the Arabic translation ʿUnf al-diktātūriyyah [The Violence of Dictatorship] of Stefan Zweig's Castellio gegen Calvin oder Ein Gewissen gegen die Gewalt as a point of reference, the author criticizes the present political situation in Iraq\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://www.m.ahewar.org/s.asp?aid=460718&r=0\n\nThis is a review of the Arabic translation:\n\nʿUnf al-diktātūriyyah [The Violence of Dictatorship = Castellio gegen Calvin oder Ein Gewissen gegen die Gewalt]. Translated by Fāris Yūwākīm [Fares Youakim]. 223p. 1st edition. Beirut: Dār al-Furāt li-l-Nashr waʾl-Tawzīʿ, 2013\n\n[2]. \"Al-Diktātūriyyah al-muzdahirah fī ʾl-ʿIrāq\" [The Flourishing Dictatorship in Iraq] in Talalsquf: thaqāfī - ijtimāʿī - siyāsī [tellskuf.com / Teleskof: Cultural - Social - Political] [Teleskof?], 26 March 2015\n\nTalalsquf is the webpage of the northern Iraqi town of \"Teleskof\", the Chaldean Catholic population of which had to flee their home town during its recent occupation by fighters of the so-called \"Islamic State\"\n\nThis is a republication of the preceding text \npublished online:\n\nhttp://www.tellskuf.com/index.php/authors/274-eq/46262-2015-03-26-19-45-48.html",
      "sourceBlobId": 3
    },
