      "name": {
        "@value": "Qirāʾah li-kitāb «Mājillān qāhir al-biḥār» li-muʾallifihī li-Stīfān Zfāyj",
        "@language": "ar"
      },
      "sourceTextId": 35100,
      "datePublished": "2010",
      "allYears": [
        2008,
        2010
      ],
      "timePeriod": "contemporary",
      "publisher": {
        "@id": "klawiter:publisher/the%20Markaz%20Aw%C4%81n%20li-l-Istish%C4%81r%C4%81t%20al-I%CA%BFl%C4%81miyyah%20al-%CA%BFArabiyyah",
        "@type": "schema:Organization",
        "name": "the Markaz Awān li-l-Istishārāt al-Iʿlāmiyyah al-ʿArabiyyah"
      },
      "locationCreated": {
        "@id": "klawiter:place/Amman",
        "@type": "schema:Place",
        "name": "Amman"
      },
      "inLanguage": "ar",
      "languageName": "Arabic",
      "numberOfPages": 143,
      "categories": [
        "Secondary Literature / Titles (Arabic)"
      ],
      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "\"Qirāʾah li-kitāb «Mājillān qāhir al-biḥār» li-muʾallifihī li(sic)-Stīfān Zfāygh\" [Review of the Book \"Conqueror of the Seas. The Story of Magellan\" by the author Stefan Zweig] in Ṣaḥafī [Journalist] [Amman], 23 April 2010\n\nṢaḥafī [Journalist] is a Jordanian website published by the Markaz Awān li-l-Istishārāt al-Iʿlāmiyyah al-ʿArabiyyah [Amman]\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://www.sahafi.jo/arc/art1.php?id=a559456faa9d81753995a4e108409d7cc7116fbe\n\nThis review, the author of which is not indicated, originally appeared in the Jordanian daily Al-Dustūr [The Constitution], Amman. It is dedicated to the Arabic translation of Magellan. Der Mann und seine Tat\n\nMājillān. Qāhir al-biḥār awwal man ṭāfa ḥawla ʾl-ʿālam waʾrtāda al-muḥīṭāt al-shāsiʿah [Magellan, Conqueror of the Seas. The First Person Who Circumnavigated the World and Explored the Wide Oceans]. Translated by Ḥabīb Jāmātī. 143p. Damascus: Dār al-Madā li-l-Thaqāfah waʾl-Nashr, 2008",
      "sourceBlobId": 3
    },
    {
      "@type": [
        "schema:ScholarlyArticle",
        "klawiter:SecondaryLiteratureEntry"
      ],
      "@id": "klawiter:entry/4920",
      "entryType": "secondary-literature",
      "sourcePageId": 4920,
      "pageNamespace": 0,
      "name": {
        "@value": "Badr, ʿAbd al-Maʿbūd",
        "@language": "ar"
      },
      "sourceTextId": 35086,
      "datePublished": "2017",
      "allYears": [
        1965,
        2017
      ],
      "timePeriod": "contemporary",
      "publisher": {
        "@id": "klawiter:publisher/house%20Al-D%C4%81r%20al-Qawmiyyah%20li-l-%E1%B9%ACib%C4%81%CA%BFah%20wa%CA%BEl-Nashr",
        "@type": "schema:Organization",
        "name": "house Al-Dār al-Qawmiyyah li-l-Ṭibāʿah waʾl-Nashr"
      },
      "locationCreated": {
        "@id": "klawiter:place/Kuwait",
        "@type": "schema:Place",
        "name": "Kuwait"
      },
      "inLanguage": "ar",
      "languageName": "Arabic",
      "categories": [
        "Secondary Literature / Authors (Arabic)"
      ],
      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "\"Durūs daʿawiyyah wa-ḥaḍāriyyah min kitāb \"Mājillān qāhir al-biḥār\"\" [Missionary and Civilizational Lessons from the Book \"Conqueror of the Seas. The Story of Magellan\"] in Mahārāt al-daʿwah [dawahskills / Missionary Skills], [Kuwait], 27 December 2017\n\nThe webpage Mahārāt al-daʿwah [dawahskills / Missionary Skills] is published by the Jamʿiyyat al-Najāt al-Khayriyyah [Al-Najat Charity], Kuwait\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://alturl.com/enrp4\n\nIn this bigoted review of the Arabic translation Mājillān. Qāhir al-biḥār: qiṣṣat awwal man ṭāfa ḥawla ʾl-arḍ [of Stefan Zweig's Magellan. Der Mann und seine Tat] neither the Austrian-Jewish author himself nor the Egyptian translator Ḥabīb Jāmātī nor the date (1965) or place of publication nor the name of the Cairene publishing house Al-Dār al-Qawmiyyah li-l-Ṭibāʿah waʾl-Nashr [National Publication & Printing House] are mentioned. Instead, the reader is told that Magellan did not discover anything new the Muslims had not already known \"more than five or six centuries\" before him by the means of Coranic and Hadith exegesis alone",
      "sourceBlobId": 3
    },
