      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "[1]. [2014]: Zytglogge Verlag, Oberhofen am Thunersee\n\n\"Wyssi Rose uf ds Grab vom Stefan Zweig\" [White Roses on Stefan Zweig's Grave] in Gerhard Binggeli. I bsinne mi. Gschichte vo hie u dert [I Remember. Stories from Here and There]. Edited by Hugo Ramseyer. Co-edited by Monika Künzi and Jakob Salzmann. 115p. [I bsinne mi (I Remember), 1]. \"Wyssi Rose uf ds Grab vom Stefan Zweig\", pp. 42-43\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttps://books.google.de/books?id=ThIRDAAAQBAJ&pg=PT43&lpg=PT43&dq=%22Gerhard+Binggeli%22+Stefan+Zweig&source=bl&ots=8Avi5LKdR4&sig=WwvHSO5BKpwbPThqJcxdD1KHlEM&hl=de&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwiG2f_i_vHZAhXSC-wKHW9LBFUQ6AEISTAK#v=onepage&q=%22Gerhard%20Binggeli%22%20Stefan%20Zweig&f=false\n\nhttps://issuu.com/zytgloggeverlag/docs/binggeli_ibsinne_leseprobe [shortened preview of the book (pp. 1-21) without the mentioned essay, but with the contents on p. 7]\n\n[2]. \"Chrieg u Fride u der Stefan Zweig. Chürzlech isch mir vom Stefan Zweig sys Buech «Welt von gestern» wider i d Finger cho, un i ha di 500 Syte verschlunge, aber sie hei mer o z'dänke gä\" [War and Peace and Stefan Zweig. Not Long Ago, I Came Again Upon Stefan Zweig's Book \"The World of Yesterday\" and I Devoured These 500 Pages. Yet, They Also Made Me Think] in Der Bund [The Union] [Bern], 30 June 2015, p. ?\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttps://www.derbund.ch/bern/stadt/Chrieg-u-Fride-u-der-Stefan-Zweig/story/27423823?dossier_id=3069\n\nThis is a review of Die Welt von Gestern. Erinnerungen eines Europäers",
      "sourceBlobId": 4
    },
