      ],
      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "\"'Risālah min imraʾah majhūlah'.. jamaʿa Farīd wa-Lubnā wa-aghḍaba Ḥalīm\" ['Letter from an Unknown Woman'... Brought Together Farīd (al-Aṭrash) and Lubnā (ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz) and Infuriated (ʿAbd al-)Ḥalīm (Ḥāfiẓ)] in Al-Ittiḥād [The Union] [Abu Dhabi], No. ? [25 December 2015], p. ?\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://www.alittihad.ae/details.php?id=115265&y=2015\n\nThis is a review of the Egyptian film \"Risālah min imraʾah majhūlah\" [Letter from an Unknown Woman] [1962], directed by Ṣalāḥ Abū Sayf, script by Fatḥī Zakī and Wafīyah Khayrī, starring Farīd al-Aṭrash, Lubnā ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, Amīnah Rizq, and Mārī Munīb. The film is an adaptation of Stefan Zweig's novella \"Brief einer Unbekannten\"",
      "sourceBlobId": 4
    },
