      ],
      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "\"7 [Sabʿ] riwāyāt tunqidhuka min qafaṣ \"al-ḥubb al-awwal\"?.. Ḥulūl sīnimāʾiyyah faʿʿālah [Seven Novels Which Preserve You from the Cage of the \"First Love\"? - Effective Solutions in Cinema] in Rūtānā [Rotana] [Abu Dhabi], 18 March 2017\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://rotana.net/7-%d8%b1%d9%88%d8%a7%d9%8a%d8%a7%d8%aa-%d8%aa%d9%86%d9%82%d8%b0%d9%83-%d9%85%d9%86-%d9%82%d9%81%d8%b5-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%ad%d8%a8-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%a3%d9%88%d9%84%d8%9f-%d8%ad%d9%84%d9%88%d9%84-%d8%b3/\n\nAmong the film versions of the seven novels and novellas which are discussed in this article is the Egyptian film \"Risālah min imraʾah majhūlah\" [Letter from an Unknown Woman] [1962], directed by Ṣalāḥ Abū Sayf, script by Fatḥī Zakī and Wafīyah Khayrī, starring Farīd al-Aṭrash, Lubnā ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, Amīnah Rizq, and Mārī Munīb. The film is an adaptation of Stefan Zweig's novella \"Brief einer Unbekannten\"",
      "sourceBlobId": 4
    },
