      ],
      "mainCategory": "Translations by Zweig",
      "bibliographicCitation": "The following editions of Les Fleurs du mal are the ones quoted in Baudelaire, Charles / Individual Poems\n\n1857: Les Fleurs du mal. 248p. Paris: Poulet-Malassis et De Broise, Libraires-Éditeurs\n1861: Les Fleurs du mal. 2nd edition. Augmented with 35 new poems. Contains a portrait of the author by Félix Bracquemond. 319p. Paris: Poulet-Malassis et De Broise, Éditeurs\n1868 [AL]: Les Fleurs du mal [Oeuvres complètes de Ch. Baudelaire. Vol. I]. (4)/382p. Introductory essay by Théophile Gautier. Paris: Alphonse Lemerre, Éditeur\n1868 [CL]: Les Fleurs du mal [Oeuvres complètes de Charles Baudelaire. Vol. I]. Introductory essay by Théophile Gautier. Definitive edition augmented with a great number of new poems. 411p. Illustrated with a portrait of Charles Baudelaire. Paris: Calmann-Lévy, Éditeurs [Michel Lévy Frères, Libraires Éditeurs]\n1930: Les Fleurs du mal / Les Épaves [Oeuvres complètes de Charles Baudelaire. Vol. I]. Introduction and notes by M. Jacques Crépet. XLI/520p. Based on the 1868 edition. Paris: Louis Conard, Libraire-Éditeur\n1942: Les Fleurs du mal [Text of the 2nd edition, followed by poems omitted in the 1857 edition and the additions in the 1868 edition]. This critical edition was edited by Jacques Crépet and Georges Blin. Paris: Librairie José Corti\n1949: Les Fleurs du mal. Preface and notes by Ernest Raynaud. LIV/332p. Paris: Librairie Garnier Frères\n1951: Les Fleurs du mal. Contains original aquarelles by Émilien Dufour. 305/(1)p. Paris: La Bonne Compagnie\n1957: Les Fleurs du mal. Text edited with an afterword by Marcel A. Ruff. Contains a colored portrait of the author by Charles Baudelaire himself. 455p. Paris: Jean-Jacques Pauvert, Éditeur\n1961: Les Fleurs du mal / Les Épaves - Bribes - Poèmes divers - Amoenitates Belgicae. Contains a portrait of Charles Baudelaire by Nadar [i.e. Gaspard-Félix Tournachon]. xix/491p. Paris: Éditions Garnier Frères\n1975. Oeuvres complètes de Charles Baudelaire. 2 vols. Vol. I contains \"Les Fleurs du mal\". Text edited with notes by Claude Pichois. Vol. I/1604p. Paris: Éditions Gallimard\n1995: Les Fleurs du mal. Edited with an introduction and notes by Graham Chesters. xx/228p. Based on the 1861 edition. London: Bristol Classical Press\n1999: Les Fleurs du mal. Edition established by John E. Jackson. Preface by Yves Bonnefoy. xvii/374p. Paris: Le Livre de Poche [classique]\n2001: Les Fleurs du mal. Lecture intégrale. Edited with a preface, an introduction and lengthy analyses of the poems by Mario Richter. 2 vols. [1705p]. Genève: Éditions Slatkine",
      "sourceBlobId": 5
    },
