      "mainCategory": "Translations by Zweig",
      "bibliographicCitation": "[1906]: Julius Zeitler Verlag, Leipzig\n\nRussell, Archibald (George Blomefield). Die visionäre Kunstphilosophie des William Blake. 30p. Portrait of William Blake on the title page. 20 copies of this edition were printed and numbered on handmade paper\n\nEnglsih original:\n\n\"The Visionary Art of William Blake\" in Edinburgh Review [London], 203:415 [January/April 1906], pp. 161-179\n\nSee also Stefan Zweig's essay:\n\n\"William Blakes Auferstehung\" in Neue Freie Presse [Wien], 27 January 1907, pp. 32-34\n\nThis essay contains reviews of the following volumes:\n\nKassner, Rudolf. Die Mystik, die Künstler und das Laben. Über englische Dichter und Maler im 19. Jahrhundert. Accorde. Leipzig: Eugen Diederichs Verlag, 1900\nRichter, Helene. William Blake. Straßburg: Heitz & Mündel Verlag, 1906\nRussell, Archibald G. B. Die visionäre Kunstphilosophie des William Blake. Leipzig: Julius Zeitler Verlag, 1906\nSwinburne, Algernon Charles. William Blake. A Critical Essay. New edition. New York: E. P. Dutton Publishing Company, 1906 [1st edition. London, 1868. Publisher not identified]\n\nZweig also discusses a William Blake Exhibition in London",
      "sourceBlobId": 5
    },
