      },
      "locationCreated": {
        "@id": "klawiter:place/Berlin",
        "@type": "schema:Place",
        "name": "Berlin",
        "sameAs": "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q64"
      },
      "allLocations": [
        "Berlin",
        "Leipzig"
      ],
      "numberOfPages": 122,
      "translator": {
        "@id": "klawiter:person/Johannes%20Schlaf",
        "@type": "schema:Person",
        "name": "Johannes Schlaf"
      },
      "categories": [
        "Forewords and Afterwords"
      ],
      "mainCategory": "Forewords and Afterwords",
      "decomposedAsWork": "klawiter:work/6477",
      "bibliographicCitation": "[1902]: Schuster & Loeffler Verlag, Berlin/Leipzig\n\nGedichte von Paul Verlaine. Eine Anthologie der besten Übertragungen. Edited with a foreword by Stefan Zweig. Portrait of Verlaine by Félix Valloton. 122/(2)p. Stefan Zweig's foreword \"Paul Verlaine\", pp. 5-21. An excerpt was printed as \"Paul Verlaine\" in Das Magazin für Litteratur [Berlin], 71:40 [4 October 1902], pp. (313)-315. Contains three translations by Stefan Zweig: \"Behutsam\", \"Einst war ich gläubig...\", and \"Die Unverdorbenen\". See Verlaine, Paul / Translations by Stefan Zweig\n\n[1907. Reprinted 1911]: Schuster & Loeffler Verlag, Berlin/Leipzig\n\nGedichte von Paul Verlaine. Eine Anthologie der besten Übertragungen. Minus Stefan Zweig's foreword but edited with a preliminary remark by Stefan Zweig. 112/(1)p. Stefan Zweig's \"Vorbemerkung\", p. (5). Contains six translations by Stefan Zweig: \"Behutsam\", \"Einst war ich gläubig...\", \"Intérieur\", \"Mondschein\", \"Regen\", and \"Die Unverdorbenen\". See Verlaine, Paul / Translations by Stefan Zweig\n\n[1922]: Insel-Verlag, Leipzig\n\nPaul Verlaines Gesammelte Werke in zwei Bänden. Edited by Stefan Zweig. Vol. 1: Gesammelte Gedichte. Eine Auswahl der besten Übertragungen [52 translators]. Afterword by Stefan Zweig. 359/(1)p. Illustrated. Stefan Zweig's afterword, p. (345). Vol. 2: Lebensdokumente. Translated by Johannes Schlaf, Hanns von Gumppenberg, and Friderike Maria Zweig. Foreword by Stefan Zweig. 415/(2)p. Stefan Zweig's \"Paul Verlaines Leben\", pp. (5)-21. Contains a photo-reproduction of a poem by Verlaine [\"Pour le Roi des Belges\"] and six of his drawings. Contains seven translations by Stefan Zweig: \"Einst war ich gläubig...\", \"Intérieur\", \"Das linde Lied\", \"Mondschein\", \"Regen\", \"Der Tod\", and \"Die Unverdorbenen\". See: Verlaine, Paul / Translations by Stefan Zweig\n\n[1927]: Insel-Verlag, Leipzig\n\nPaul Verlaine. Gedichte. Eine Auswahl der besten Übertragungen. Complied with an afterword by Stefan Zweig. 71/(1)p. [Insel-Bücherei, 394]. Stefan Zweig's afterword, pp. 69-70 [In the 1938 edition, pp. 61-62]. Contains three translations by Stefan Zweig: \"Das linde Lied\", \"Mondschein\", and \"Regen\". See: Verlaine, Paul / Translations by Stefan Zweig\n\n*1st edition. 10,000 copies. 1927\n*2nd edition. 5,000 copies. 1929\n*3rd edition. 5,000 copies. 1931\n*4th edition. 3,000 copies. 1938 [63/(1)p. Minus Stefan Zweig's translations]",
      "sourceBlobId": 5
    },
