      ],
      "mainCategory": "Secondary Literature",
      "bibliographicCitation": "\"Duniya ko dekhane ka najariya\" [View of the World], in: Oma Sharma's Blog [Santa Cruz, CA], 05 December 2016\n\nPublished online:\n\nhttp://omasharma.com/reviews-of-my-books/%E0%A4%A6%E0%A5%81%E0%A4%A8%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%AF%E0%A4%BE-%E0%A4%95%E0%A5%8B-%E0%A4%A6%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%96%E0%A4%A8%E0%A5%87-%E0%A4%95%E0%A4%BE-%E0%A4%A8%E0%A4%9C%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%AF%E0%A4%BE/2016/12/05/\n\nThis is a review of Oma Sharma's [Omā Śarmā] travel diary \"Antaryatrayen : vaaya Viyana\" [Intervals: via Vienna]. Panchkula: Ādhāra Prakāśana [Aadhar Prakashan Pvt. Ltd.], 2016, which comprises eight essays by the Hindi author and Zweig translator Oma Sharma. Sharma recounts his travel experiences in India and Europe, inter alia, an extensive essay (ca. 70p.) about Vienna and Austria as the cultural setting of Stefan Zweig's œuvre.",
      "sourceBlobId": 5
    },
