      "bibliographicCitation": "[1996]: Éditions Labor et Archives et Musée de la Littérature, Bruxelles\n\nÉmile Verhaeren. Correspondance générale I: Émile et Marthe Verhaeren - Stefan Zweig (1900-1926). Edition established and presented with an introduction and notes by Fabrice van de Kerckhove. 606/(2)p.\n\nContents:\n\n(Préface) [Fabrice van de Kerckhove], pp. (5)-6\nIntroduction [Fabrice van de Kerckhove], pp. (7)-91\nL'édition, pp. 92-94\nAbréviations, pp. 95-100\nCorrespondance Émile et Marthe Verhaeren - Stefan Zweig, pp. 101-526\nBibliographie, pp. (527)-547\nTables, chronologie et index, pp. (549)-606\n::[1]. Poèmes de Verhaeren traduits par Zweig, pp. 551-553\n::[2]. Repères chronologiques, pp. 555-566\n::[3]. Table des lettres et des documents, pp. 567-574\n::[4]. Index des noms, pp. 575-588\n::[5]. Index des titres, pp. 589-606\n\nTable, p. (607)\n \n\nCorrespondance Émile et Marthe Verhaeren - Stefan Zweig\n\n1900, p. (103)\n::Émile Verhaeren to Stefan Zweig, 1 letter, 15 October \n\n1903, pp. (105)-122\n::Émile Verhaeren to Stefan Zweig, 8 letters, 12 June-22 December\n::Stefan Zweig to Émile Verhaeren, 3 letters, November, 19 December, 31 December\n\n1904, pp. (123)-152\n::Émile Verhaeren to Stefan Zweig, 27 letters, 7 January-24 December\nStefan Zweig to Émile Verhaeren, 2 letters, 28 January, 7 February\n\n1905, pp. (153)-175\n::Émile Verhaeren to Stefan Zweig, 16 letters, 8 January-31 December\n::Stefan Zweig to Émile Verhaeren, 2 letters, 3 September, 29 October\n\n1906, pp. (177)-185\n::Émile Verhaeren to Stefan Zweig, 6 letters, March-29 December\n::Ellen Key, Erna Rehwoldt & Émile Verhaeren to Stefan Zweig, 1 letter, 13 June\n::Stefan Zweig to Émile Verhaeren, 1 letter, July\n\n1907, pp. (187)-199\n::Émile Verhaeren to Stefan Zweig, 9 letters, 14 April-12 December\n\n1908, pp. (201)-217\n::Émile Verhaeren to Stefan Zweig, 9 letters, 3 January-28 October\n::Marthe and Émile Verhaeren to Stefan Zweig, 1 letter, 21 August\n::Marthe Verhaeren to Stefan Zweig, 1 letter, 21 September\n\n1909, pp. (218)-246\n::Émile Verhaeren to Stefan Zweig, 18 letters, 13 March-6 December\n::Stefan Zweig to Émile Verhaeren, 3 letters, 27 August, 2 November, 4 December\n\n1910, pp. (247)-324\n::Émile Verhaeren to Stefan Zweig, 41 letters, 3 January-12 December\n::Stefan Zweig to Émile Verhaeren, 11 letters, 6 January-31 December\n::Émile and Marthe Verhaeren to Stefan Zweig, 1 letter, 25 May\n::Marthe Verhaeren to Stefan Zweig, 2 letters, 9 October, 18 November\n::Stefan Zweig to Marthe Verhaeren, 1 letter, 12 October\n\n1911, pp. (325)-373\n::Émile Verhaeren to Stefan Zweig, 23 letters, 2 January-28 December\n::Stefan Zweig to Émile Verhaeren, 7 letters, mid January-mid December\n::Marthe and Émile Verhaeren to Stefan Zweig, 1 letter, 18 December\n\n1912, pp. (375)-441\n::Émile Verhaeren to Stefan Zweig, 30 letters, 2 February-29 December\n::Stefan Zweig to Émile Verhaeren, 12 letters, 3 January-end of December\n::Marthe Verhaeren to Stefan Zweig, 2 letters, 25 February, 9 March\n\n1913, pp. (443)-(478)\n::Émile Verhaeren to Stefan Zweig, 20 Letters, 1 February-27 December\n::Stefan Zweig to Émile Verhaeren, 3 letters, 9 January, 14 February, September/October\n::Émile Verhaeren, Rainer Maria Rilke, and Anton Kippenberg to Stefan Zweig, 1 letter, 19 November\n\n1914, pp. (479)-491\n::Émile Verhaeren and Oskar Fried to Stefan Zweig, 1 letter, 3 February\n::Émile Verhaeren to Stefan Zweig, 11 letters, 27 February-16 July\n::Stefan Zweig to Émile Verhaeren, 2 letters, end of May-ca. 12 June\n\n1923, pp. (519)-522\n::Stefan Zweig to Marthe Verhaeren, 1 letter, 29 November\n\n1926, pp. (523)-524\n::Stefan Zweig to Marthe Verhaeren, 1 letter, 5 October\n\n1929, pp. (525)-526\n::Stefan Zweig to Marthe Verhaeren, 1 letter, 19 October\n\n1914-1923, pp. (493)-517 / Historical and Literary references\n::1914, pp. (493)-504\n::1915, pp. 505-509\n::1916, pp. 510-513\n::1917, pp. 513-515\n::1918, pp. 515-516\n::1919, p. 516\n::1920, p. 516\n::1921, p. 516\n::1922, p. 516\n::1923, p. 517\n\n[2012]: Archives et Musée de la Littérature, Bruxelles\n\nCorrespondance générale: Vol. 2, Émile et Marthe Verhaeren, Richard et Ida Dehmel, Rainer Maria Rilke (1905-1925). Edited with notes by Fabrice van de Kerckhove. 237/(1)p. Illustrated. The cover contains a 1912 photograph of Emile Verhaeren by Rudolph Dührkoop\n\nContents:\n\nAvant-propos, p. (5)\nRemerciements, p. (7)\nNote sur les manuscrits et l'édition, pp. (9)-10\nCorrespondance avec Richard et Ida Dehmel, pp. (11)-21\nCorrespondance avec Rainer Maria Rilke, pp. (23)-61\nPostface, pp. (77)-191: Dehmel et Verhaeren: \"Nous les ingénieurs des 'Forces tumultueuses'\", pp. 87-117; Rilke et Verhaeren: \"Cette voix fidèle qui, de son arc-en-ciel, supprime l'abîme\", pp. 118-191\nChronologie, pp. (193)-211\nListe des illustrations, pp. (213)-215\nAbréviations et repères bibliographiques, pp. (217)-225\nIndex des noms, pp. (227)-233\nTable des matières, pp. (235)-237\n\nStefan Zweig references:\n\n[1]: Letters: [1]. Émile Verhaeren, Stefan Zweig and Franz Servaes to Richard Dehmel [Wien, March 1912], p. 19, Note 3, pp. 19-20. [2]. Julius Bab, Émile Verhaeren and Stefan Zweig to Richard Dehmel [Le Caillou-qui-bique, between 18 and 25 August, 1912], p. 20, Notes 1 &2, p. 20. [3]. Émile Verhaeren and Stefan Zweig to Rainer Maria Rilke [Roisin, 13 August 1908], p. 44, Notes 1-3, pp. 44-45\n\n[2]: \"La mediation de Stefan Zweig\" [Fabrice van de Kerckhove], pp. 87-92\n\n[3]: Index des noms, p. 233: ZWEIG, STEFAN, pp. (5), (7), 14, 15, 17, 18, 19, 20, 26, 29, 30, 38, 39, 40, 42, 44, 45, 46, 47, 49, 50, 84, 86, 87, 93, 94, 97, 98, 100, 101, 104, 105, 107, 108, 109, 110, 113, 114, 115, 117, 121, 125, 126, 129, 148, 154, 157, 158, 160, 161, 162, 163, 170, 173, 174, 177, 183, 190, 196, 198, 199, 200, 201, 202, 203, 204, 206, 207, 208, 213, 215\n\n[4]: See also p. 219 [Correspondances d'Émile Verhaeren - Verhaeren/Zweig]; p. 224 [Correspondances de Rainer Maria Rilke - Rilke/Zweig]; p. 225 [Correspondances et oeuvres de Stefan Zweig]",
