      "bibliographicCitation": "[2020]: Pushkin Press, London\n\nStefan Zweig. Encounters and Destinies. A Farewell to Europe. Edited, translated, and with an introduction by Will Stone. 249/(7)p.\n\nContents:\n\nIntroduction [Will Stone, Exmoor, 2020], pp. 9-25\nThe Return of Gustav Mahler (1915), pp. (27)-39 [\"Gustav Mahlers Wiederkehr\" in Neue Freie Presse [Wien], 25 April 1915, pp. (1)-4]\nMemories of Emile Verhaeren (1917), pp. (41)-99 [\"Erinnerungen an Emile Verhaeren\". A private printing, Wien, 1917]\nArthur Schnitzler on His Sixtieth Birthday (1922), pp. (101)-106 [\"Arthur Schnitzler. Zu seinem sechzigsten Geburtstag 15. Mai 1922\" in Neue Rundschau [Berlin], 33:5 [May 1922], pp. 498-513. Stefan Zweig's contribution, pp. 510-513]\nFrans Masereel. Man and Creator (1923), pp. (107)-119 [\"Frans Masereel. Der Man und Bildner\" in Neue Freie Presse [Wien], 4 November 1923], pp. (1)-4\nMarcel Proust's Tragic Life Course (1925), pp. (121)-130 [\"Marcel Prousts tragischer Lebenslauf\" in Neue Freie Presse [Wien], 27 September 1925, pp. 27-28]\nA Thank You to Romain Rolland (1926), pp. (131)-135 [\"(Dank an Romain Rolland)\" in \"Dichter und Denker über Romain Rolland. (Huldigungen zum sechzigsten Geburtstage, 29. Januar 1926)\" in Neue Freie Presse [Wien], 24 January 1926, pp. 29-30. Stefan Zweig's contribution, p. 30]\nA Farewell to Rilke (Speech Given at the Munich Staatstheater) (1927), pp. (137)-155 [\"Gedenkrede für Rainer Maria Rilke\" (Address delivered at the Münchner Staatstheater, 20 February 1927)] in Neue Freie Presse [Wien], 20 February 1927, pp. (1)-4. Expanded version: Abschied von Rilke. Eine Rede. 30p. Tübingen: Wunderlich Verlag, (1928)]\nNotes on Joyce's Ulysses (1928), pp. (157)-163 [\"Anmerkung zum Ulysses\" in Die Neue Rundschau [Berlin], 39:10 [October 1928], pp. (476)-479]\nAddress to Honour Maxim Gorky (On the Poet's Sixtieth Birthday) (1928), pp. (165)-177 [\"Rede zu Ehren Maxim Gorkis - Zum sechzigsten Geburtstag des Dichters, 26. März 1928\" in Neue Freie Presse [Wien], 25 March 1928, pp. 31-32\nHugo von Hofmannsthal (Speech Given at the Commemorative Ceremony Organized by the Vienna Burgtheater in Honor of the Poet) (1929], pp. (179)-193 [\"Hugo von Hofmannsthal. Gedächtnisrede zur Trauerfeier im Wiener Burgtheater , October 1929]\nArturo Toscanini. A Life Portrait (1935), pp. (195)-207 [Arturo Toscanini. Ein Bildnis. Wien: Herbert Reichner Verlag, 1935]\nMater Dolorosa (Letters from Nietzsche's Mother to Overbeck) (1937) [\"Mater Dolorosa: Die Briefe von Nietzsches Mutter an Overbeck\" in Neues Wiener Tageblatt [Wien], 21 December 1937, pp. 2-3]\nA Farewell to John Drinkwater (1937), pp. (219)-224 [\"Schattenspiel des Lebens\" in Neues Wiener Journal [Wien], 28 March 1937, p. 8]\nJoseph Roth (Address to the Funeral Service / A eulogy, Conway Hall, London, 24 June 1939) (1939), pp. {225)-239 [\"Joseph Roth: Ansprache zur Trauerfeier\" in Österreichische Post [Paris], 1 July 1939, pp. (1)-2]\nWords spoken at the Casket of Sigmund Freud (1939), pp. (241)-246 [\"Worte am Sarge Sigmund Freuds\" (Gesprochen, am 26. September 1939 im Krematorium (Golders Green), London]. 100 copies printed. Amsterdam: Uitgeverji Allert de Lange, 1939\nDetails of First Publication, pp. 247-248\nTranslator's Acknowledgements, p. 249\nBiographical data concerning Will Stone, p. (250)\nMore from Stefan Zweig, p. (251)-(256). Pages (252)-(256) contain photographs of the front covers of five other Stefan Zweig books published by the Pushkin Press: [1]. The World of Yesterday: Memoirs of a European. [2]. Beware of Pity. [3]. The Collected Novellas of Stefan Zweig. [4]. Journeys. [5]. Nietzsche",
